 or care pathway step not captured in other fields.</items><items id="text">Comment</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0006"><items id="comment">Use this data element to record simple terms or precoordinated complications. For example: Hematuria after a kidney biopsy, tissue irritation after insertion of intravenous catheter. If the requirements for recording complication are more complex then use of a specific CLUSTER archetype within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype is advised and this data element becomes redundant.</items><items id="description">Details about any complication arising from the procedure.</items><items id="text">Complication</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0007"><items id="description">Request for procedure sent.</items><items id="text">Procedure request sent</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0014"><items id="comment">For example: the reason for the cancellation or suspension of the procedure.</items><items id="description">Reason that the activity or care pathway step for the identified procedure was carried out.</items><items id="text">Reason</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0034"><items id="comment">(Was: The procedure to be undertaken is planned.)</items><items id="description">This pathway step has been deprecated as it was incorrectly associated with 'initial' status - use the new 'Procedure planned' (at0004) pathway step  which is correctly associated with 'planned' status.</items><items id="text">X - Procedure planned</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0035"><items id="comment">(Was: Request for procedure sent.)</items><items id="description">This pathway step has been deprecated as it was incorrectly associated with 'initial' status - use the new 'Procedure request sent' (at0007) pathway step  which is correctly associated with 'planned' status.</items><items id="text">X - Procedure request sent</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0036"><items id="description">The procedure has been scheduled.</items><items id="text">Procedure scheduled</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0038"><items id="description">The procedure has been postponed.</items><items id="text">Procedure postponed</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0039"><items id="description">The planned procedure has been cancelled prior to commencement.</items><items id="text">Procedure cancelled</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0040"><items id="description">The procedure has been suspended.</items><items id="text">Procedure suspended</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0041"><items id="description">The procedure has been aborted.</items><items id="text">Procedure aborted</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0043"><items id="description">The procedure has been performed and all associated clinical activities completed.</items><items id="text">Procedure completed</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0047"><items id="description">The procedure, or subprocedure in a multicomponent procedure, has been performed.</items><items id="text">Procedure performed</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0048"><items id="comment">Coding of the 'Outcome' with a terminology is recommended, if available.</items><items id="description">Outcome of procedure performed.</items><items id="text">Outcome</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0049"><items id="comment">For example: description about the performance and findings from the the procedure, the aborted attempt or the cancellation of the procedure.</items><items id="description">Narrative description about the procedure, as appropriate for the pathway step.</items><items id="text">Description</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0053"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0054"><items id="comment">This is equivalent to Placer Order Number in HL7 v2 specifications.</items><items id="description">The local ID assigned to the order by the healthcare provider or organisation requesting the service.</items><items id="text">Requestor order identifier</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0055"><items id="description">Details about the healthcare provider or organisation requesting the service.</items><items id="text">Requestor</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0056"><items id="comment">This is equivalent to Filler Order Number in HL7 v2 specifications.</items><items id="description">The ID assigned to the order by the healthcare provider or organisation receiving the request for service. This is also referred to as Filler Order Identifier.</items><items id="text">Receiver order identifier</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0057"><items id="description">Details about the healthcare provider or organisation receiving the request for service.</items><items id="text">Receiver</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0058"><items id="comment">Coding of the 'Urgency' with a terminology is recommended, if available.</items><items id="description">Urgency of the procedure.</items><items id="text">Urgency</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0060"><items id="comment">Only for use in association with the 'Procedure performed' pathway step, and in situations where the procedure is repeated on multiple occasions before being completed or there are multiple components to the whole procedure. This may be the same as the RM time attribute for the 'Procedure completed' pathway step.</items><items id="description">The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the last component of a multicomponent procedure, was finished.</items><items id="text">End datetime</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0061"><items id="comment">Only for use in association with the 'Procedure completed' pathway steps.</items><items id="description">The total amount of time taken to complete the procedure, which may include time spent during the active phase of the procedure plus time during which the procedure was suspended.</items><items id="text">Total duration</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0062"><items id="description">Mulitimedia representation of a performed procedure.</items><items id="text">Multimedia</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0063"><items id="comment">Occurrences for this data element are unbounded to allow for clinical scenarios such as removing multiple skin lesions in different places, but where all of the other attributes are identical. Use this data element to record simple terms or precoordinated anatomical locations. If the requirements for recording the anatomical location are determined at run-time by the application or require more complex modelling such as relative locations then use the CLUSTER.anatomical_location or CLUSTER.relative_location within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype. If the anatomical location is included in the 'Procedure name' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant.</items><items id="description">Identification of the body site for the procedure.</items><items id="text">Body site</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0064"><items id="comment">For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR.</items><items id="description">Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms.</items><items id="text">Extension</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0065"><items id="comment">Use this data element to record simple terms or a narrative description. If the requirements for recording the method require more complex modelling then this can be represented by additional archetypes within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype. If the method is included in the 'Procedure name' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant.</items><items id="description">Identification of specific method or technique for the procedure.</items><items id="text">Method</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0066"><items id="comment">Only for use in association with the 'Procedure scheduled' pathway step.</items><items id="description">The date or datetime on which the procedure is intended to be performed.</items><items id="text">Scheduled datetime</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0067"><items id="comment">This pragmatic data element may be used to support organisation within the user interface.</items><items id="description">The type of procedure.</items><items id="text">Procedure type</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0068"><items id="description">The procedure, or subprocedure in a multicomponent procedure, has been commenced.</items><items id="text">Procedure commenced</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0069"><items id="comment">Examples: The patient was agitated, insufficient emptying of the stomach before gastroscopy, a tumour in the bile ducts made it impossible to pass the scope through.</items><items id="description">Difficulties or issues encountered during performance of the procedure.</items><items id="text">Procedural difficulty</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0070"><items id="comment">For example: 'Failed bowel preparation' or 'Bowel cancer screening'. Coding of the 'Indication' with a terminology is recommended, if available.  This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required.</items><items id="description">The clinical or process-related reason for the procedure.</items><items id="text">Indication</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0071"><items id="comment">The same procedure, with the same severity or outcome, can have a different impact on each patient. This relevance factor involves adjusting the overall impact of that procedure or outcome according to the patient's characteristics.&#13;
&#13;
For example: Two patients have undergone the same procedure with the same outcome: osteosynthesis repair of the fifth finger of their non-dominant hand.&#13;
&#13;
One is a gardener or construction worker; the other, a pianist.&#13;
&#13;
The impact of that procedure on the pianist is GREATER (longer sick leave, need for full functional rehabilitation to adapt to the high fine motor demands of work).&#13;
&#13;
This element is intended to allow for multiple types of impact, including but not limited to: clinical treatment, home functioning, or work life.</items><items id="description">Assessment of the impact of a procedure or its outcome for a specific patient.</items><items id="text">Impact</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0072"><items id="comment">For example: An operation with curative intent may be planned, while during the operation it is discovered that curative treatment is not possible and the operation is carried out with a palliative intent instead. Coding of the 'Intent' with a terminology is recommended, if available. This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required.</items><items id="description">The intended outcome of the procedure.</items><items id="text">Intent</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0073"><items id="comment">For example: the knife to skin time. Only for use in association with the 'Procedure performed', 'Procedure suspended', 'Procedure aborted' or 'Procedure completed' pathway steps. This may be the same as the RM 'time' attribute for the 'Procedure commenced' pathway step.</items><items id="description">The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the first component of a multicomponent procedure, was first started.</items><items id="text">Start datetime</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0074"><items id="description">The duration of time between the start of the most recent pathway step for this procedure and the start of the current pathway step.</items><items id="text">Pathway step duration</items></term_definitions></children><cardinality><is_ordered>true</is_ordered><is_unique>false</is_unique><interval><lower_included>true</lower_included><upper_included>true</upper_included><lower_unbounded>false</lower_unbounded><upper_unbounded>true</upper_unbounded><lower>0</lower></interval></cardinality></attributes><archetype_id><value>openEHR-EHR-COMPOSITION.encounter.v1</value></archetype_id><term_definitions code="at0000"><items id="description">Interaction, contact or care event between a subject of care and healthcare provider(s).</items><items id="text">Encounter</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></term_definitions><term_definitions code="at0002"><items id="comment">For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR.</items><items id="description">Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms.</items><items id="text">Extension</items></term_definitions></definition><ontology archetype_id="openEHR-EHR-COMPOSITION.encounter.v1"><term_definitions language="ar-sy"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">*Interaction, contact or care event between a subject of care and healthcare provider(s).(en)</items><items id="text">*Encounter(en)</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">*@ internal @(en)</items><items id="text">*Tree(en)</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">*Extension(en)</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="ca"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Interacció, contacte o esdeveniment d’atenció entre un pacient i un o més professionals d'atenció sanitària.</items><items id="text">Encontre</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">Extensió</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="de"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Interaktion, Kontakt oder Versorgungsereignis, zwischen einem Versorgungsempfänger und einem Gesundheitsdienstleister.</items><items id="text">Kontakt</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">Erweiterung</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="en"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Interaction, contact or care event between a subject of care and healthcare provider(s).</items><items id="text">Encounter</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR.</items><items id="description">Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms.</items><items id="text">Extension</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="es"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Interacción, contacto o evento de cuidado entre un paciente y un proveedor de salud.</items><items id="text">Encuentro</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">Extensión</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="es-ar"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Interacción, contacto o evento de cuidados entre un sujeto de cuidados y uno o más proveedores de cuidados de la salud.</items><items id="text">Encuentro</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">*@ internal @(en)</items><items id="text">*Tree(en)</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">Extensión</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="fi"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Hoitohenkilön ja terveydenhuollon tarjoajan välinen vuorovaikutus, kontakti- tai hoitotapahtuma.</items><items id="text">Kontakti</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">Laajennus</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="fr"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Interaction, contact ou événement de soins entre un sujet de soins et un ou des prestataires de soins.</items><items id="text">Rencontre</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">Extension</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="it"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Interazione, contatto o evento di cura tra un soggetto di cura e il/i fornitore/i di assistenza sanitaria.</items><items id="text">Contatto</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">Estensione</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="ko"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">*Interaction, contact or care event between a subject of care and healthcare provider(s).(en)</items><items id="text">*Encounter(en)</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">*@ internal @(en)</items><items id="text">*Tree(en)</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">*Extension(en)</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="nb"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Interaksjon, kontakt eller omsorgshendelse mellom et individ og helsepersonell.</items><items id="text">Klinisk kontakt</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">For eksempel lokale informasjonsbehov eller ytterligere metadata for å kunne tilpasse til tilsvarende konsepter i FHIR.</items><items id="description">Ytterligere informasjon som trengs for å kunne registrere lokalt definert innhold eller for å tilpasse til andre referansemodeller/formalismer.</items><items id="text">Utvidelse</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="nl"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Interactie, contact of zorggebeurtenis tussen een onderwerp van zorg en zorgverlener(s).</items><items id="text">Contact</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">Extensie</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="pt-br"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Interação, contato ou cuidado entre o sujeito do cuidado e profissional(is) de saúde.</items><items id="text">Encontro</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">Extensão</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="pt-pt"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Interação, contato ou evento de cuidados entre um sujeito e um provedor de saúde.</items><items id="text">Encontro</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">Extensão</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="sv"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Kontakt mellan patient och vårdgivare, eller vårdhändelse inom hälso- och sjukvården.</items><items id="text">Vårdkontakt</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">Exempelvis lokala informationskrav eller metadata för anpassning till FHIR.</items><items id="description">Plats för tilläggsinformation som krävs för lokala anpassningar eller anpassning till andra referensmodeller eller formella krav.</items><items id="text">Tilläggsinformation</items></items></term_definitions></ontology><component_ontologies archetype_id="openEHR-EHR-ACTION.procedure.v1"><term_definitions language="ar-sy"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">*A clinical activity carried out for screening, investigative, diagnostic, curative, therapeutic, evaluative or palliative purposes.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure(en)</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Procedure name' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">*Identification of the procedure by name.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure name(en)</items></items><items code="at0003"><items id="description">*Structured information about the procedure. Use to capture detailed, structured information about anatomical location, method &amp; technique, equipment used, devices implanted, results, findings etc.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure detail(en)</items></items><items code="at0004"><items id="description">*</items><items id="text">*Procedure planned (en)</items></items><items code="at0005"><items id="description">*Additional narrative about the procedure or care pathway step not captured in other fields. (en)</items><items id="text">*Comment(en)</items></items><items code="at0006"><items id="comment">*Use this data element to record simple terms or precoordinated complications. For example: Hematuria after a kidney biopsy, tissue irritation after insertion of intravenous catheter. If the requirements for recording complication are more complex then use of a specific CLUSTER archetype within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype is advised and this data element becomes redundant. (en)</items><items id="description">*Details about any complication arising from the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Complication(en)</items></items><items code="at0007"><items id="description">*</items><items id="text">*Procedure request sent (en)</items></items><items code="at0014"><items id="comment">*For example: the reason for the cancellation or suspension of the procedure.(en)</items><items id="description">*Reason that the activity or care pathway step for the identified procedure was carried out.(en)</items><items id="text">*Reason(en)</items></items><items code="at0034"><items id="description">*The procedure to be undertaken is planned.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure planned(en)</items></items><items code="at0035"><items id="description">*Request for procedure sent.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure request sent(en)</items></items><items code="at0036"><items id="description">*The procedure has been scheduled.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure scheduled(en)</items></items><items code="at0038"><items id="description">*The procedure has been postponed.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure postponed(en)</items></items><items code="at0039"><items id="description">*The planned procedure has been cancelled prior to commencement.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure cancelled(en)</items></items><items code="at0040"><items id="description">*The procedure has been suspended.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure suspended(en)</items></items><items code="at0041"><items id="description">*The procedure has been aborted.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure aborted(en)</items></items><items code="at0043"><items id="description">*The procedure has been performed and all associated clinical activities completed.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure completed(en)</items></items><items code="at0047"><items id="description">*The procedure, or subprocedure in a multicomponent procedure, has been performed.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure performed(en)</items></items><items code="at0048"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Outcome' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">*Outcome of procedure performed.(en)</items><items id="text">*Outcome(en)</items></items><items code="at0049"><items id="comment">*For example: description about the performance and findings from the the procedure, the aborted attempt or the cancellation of the procedure.(en)</items><items id="description">*Narrative description about the procedure, as appropriate for the pathway step.(en)</items><items id="text">*Description(en)</items></items><items code="at0053"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0054"><items id="comment">*This is equivalent to Placer Order Number in HL7 v2 specifications.(en)</items><items id="description">*The local ID assigned to the order by the healthcare provider or organisation requesting the service.(en)</items><items id="text">*Requestor order identifier(en)</items></items><items code="at0055"><items id="description">تفاصيل حول مقدم الخدمة الصحية أو المؤسسة التي تطلب الخدمة</items><items id="text">الطالب</items></items><items code="at0056"><items id="comment">*This is equivalent to Filler Order Number in HL7 v2 specifications.(en)</items><items id="description">*The ID assigned to the order by the healthcare provider or organisation receiving the request for service. This is also referred to as Filler Order Identifier.(en)</items><items id="text">*Receiver order identifier(en)</items></items><items code="at0057"><items id="description">تفاصيل حول مقدم الخدمة الصحية أو المؤسسة التي تستقبل طلب الخدمة.</items><items id="text">المستقبِل</items></items><items code="at0058"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Urgency' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">*Urgency of the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Urgency(en)</items></items><items code="at0060"><items id="comment">*Only for use in association with the 'Procedure performed' pathway step, and in situations where the procedure is repeated on multiple occasions before being completed or there are multiple components to the whole procedure. This may be the same as the RM time attribute for the 'Procedure completed' pathway step.(en)</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the last component of a multicomponent procedure, was finished. (en)</items><items id="text">*End datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0061"><items id="comment">*Only for use in association with the 'Procedure completed' pathway steps.(en)</items><items id="description">*The total amount of time taken to complete the procedure, which may include time spent during the active phase of the procedure plus time during which the procedure was suspended.(en)</items><items id="text">*Total duration(en)</items></items><items code="at0062"><items id="description">*Mulitimedia representation of a performed procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Multimedia(en)</items></items><items code="at0063"><items id="comment">*Occurrences for this data element are unbounded to allow for clinical scenarios such as removing multiple skin lesions in different places, but where all of the other attributes are identical. Use this data element to record simple terms or precoordinated anatomical locations. If the requirements for recording the anatomical location are determined at run-time by the application or require more complex modelling such as relative locations then use the CLUSTER.anatomical_location or CLUSTER.relative_location within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype. If the anatomical location is included in the 'Procedure name' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant.(en)</items><items id="description">*Identification of the body site for the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Body site(en)</items></items><items code="at0064"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">*Extension(en)</items></items><items code="at0065"><items id="comment">*Use this data element to record simple terms or a narrative description. If the requirements for recording the method require more complex modelling then this can be represented by additional archetypes within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype. If the method is included in the 'Procedure name' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant.(en)</items><items id="description">*Identification of specific method or technique for the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Method(en)</items></items><items code="at0066"><items id="comment">*Only for use in association with the 'Procedure scheduled' pathway step.(en)</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime on which the procedure is intended to be performed. (en)</items><items id="text">*Scheduled datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0067"><items id="comment">*This pragmatic data element may be used to support organisation within the user interface.(en)</items><items id="description">*The type of procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure type(en)</items></items><items code="at0068"><items id="description">*The procedure, or subprocedure in a multicomponent procedure, has been commenced.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure commenced(en)</items></items><items code="at0069"><items id="description">*Difficulties or issues encountered during the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedural difficulty(en)</items></items><items code="at0070"><items id="comment">*For example: 'Failed bowel preparation' or 'Bowel cancer screening'. Coding of the 'Indication' with a terminology is recommended, if available.  This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required. (en)</items><items id="description">*The clinical or process-related reason for the procedure. (en)</items><items id="text">*Indication (en)</items></items><items code="at0071"><items id="description"/><items id="text">*DV_TEXT (en)</items></items><items code="at0072"><items id="comment">*For example: An operation with curative intent may be planned, while during the operation it is discovered that curative treatment is not possible and the operation is carried out with a palliative intent instead. Coding of the 'Intent' with a terminology is recommended, if available. This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required. (en)</items><items id="description">*The intended outcome of the procedure. (en)</items><items id="text">*Intent (en)</items></items><items code="at0073"><items id="comment">*For example: the knife to skin time. Only for use in association with the 'Procedure performed', 'Procedure suspended', 'Procedure aborted' or 'Procedure completed' pathway steps. This may be the same as the RM 'time' attribute for the 'Procedure commenced' pathway step. (en)</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the first component of a multicomponent procedure, was first started. (en)</items><items id="text">*Start datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0074"><items id="description">*The duration of time between the start of the most recent pathway step for this procedure and the start of the current pathway step. (en)</items><items id="text">*Pathway step duration (en)</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="ca"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Activitat clínica duta a terme amb fins de cribratge, investigació, diagnòstic, curatius, terapèutics, d'avaluació o pal·liatius.</items><items id="text">Procediment</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Procedure name' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">Identificació del procediment pel nom.</items><items id="text">Nom del procediment</items></items><items code="at0003"><items id="comment">S'utilitza per recopilar informació detallada i estructurada sobre la localització anatòmica, el mètode i la tècnica, l'equip utilitzat, els dispositius implantats, els resultats, les troballes, etc.</items><items id="description">Informació estructurada sobre el procediment.</items><items id="text">Detalls del procediment</items></items><items code="at0004"><items id="description">Es planifica el procediment que cal dur a terme.</items><items id="text">Procediment planificat</items></items><items code="at0005"><items id="description">*Additional narrative about the procedure or care pathway step not captured in other fields. (en)</items><items id="text">Comentaris</items></items><items code="at0006"><items id="comment">*Use this data element to record simple terms or precoordinated complications. For example: Hematuria after a kidney biopsy, tissue irritation after insertion of intravenous catheter. If the requirements for recording complication are more complex then use of a specific CLUSTER archetype within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype is advised and this data element becomes redundant. (en)</items><items id="description">Detalls sobre qualsevol complicació derivada del procediment.</items><items id="text">Complicació</items></items><items code="at0007"><items id="description">Sol·licitud de procediment enviada.</items><items id="text">Sol·licitud de procediment enviada</items></items><items code="at0014"><items id="comment">Per exemple: motiu de la cancel·lació o suspensió del procediment.</items><items id="description">Motiu pel qual es va dur a terme l'activitat o etapa assistencial per al procediment identificat.</items><items id="text">Motiu</items></items><items code="at0034"><items id="comment">(Obsolet: Es planifica el procediment a dur a terme.)</items><items id="description">Aquest apartat ha quedat obsolet, ja que s'associava incorrectament amb l'estat inicial. Utilitzeu el nou apartat "Procediment planificat" (at0004), associat correctament amb l'estat "planificat".</items><items id="text">X - Procediment planificat</items></items><items code="at0035"><items id="comment">(Obsolet: Sol·licitud de procediment enviada.)</items><items id="description">Aquest apartat ha quedat obsolet, ja que s'associava incorrectament amb l'estat inicial. Utilitzeu el nou apartat "Sol·licitud de procediment enviada" (at0004), associat correctament amb l'estat "planificat".</items><items id="text">X - Sol·licitud de procediment enviada</items></items><items code="at0036"><items id="description">El procediment s'ha programat.</items><items id="text">Procediment programat</items></items><items code="at0038"><items id="description">El procediment s'ha posposat.</items><items id="text">Procediment posposat</items></items><items code="at0039"><items id="description">S'ha cancel·lat el procediment previst abans de començar.</items><items id="text">Procediment cancel·lat</items></items><items code="at0040"><items id="description">El procediment s'ha suspès.</items><items id="text">Procediment suspès</items></items><items code="at0041"><items id="description">El procediment s'ha interromput.</items><items id="text">Procediment interromput</items></items><items code="at0043"><items id="description">S'ha fet el procediment i s'han completat totes les activitats clíniques associades.</items><items id="text">Procediment completat</items></items><items code="at0047"><items id="description">El procediment o subprocediment en un procediment multicomponent s'ha realitzat.</items><items id="text">Procediment realitzat</items></items><items code="at0048"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Outcome' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">Resultat del procediment realitzat.</items><items id="text">Resultat</items></items><items code="at0049"><items id="comment">Per exemple: descripció de la realització i resultats del procediment, l'intent interromput o la cancel·lació del procediment.</items><items id="description">Descripció narrativa del procediment, segons correspongui a la fase del procés.</items><items id="text">Descripció</items></items><items code="at0053"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0054"><items id="comment">Equivalent al Placer Order Number a les especificacions HL7 v2.</items><items id="description">L'ID local assignat a l'ordre pel proveïdor sanitari o l'organització que sol·licita el servei.</items><items id="text">Identificador d'ordre del sol·licitant</items></items><items code="at0055"><items id="description">Dades del professional sanitari o organització que sol·licita el servei.</items><items id="text">Sol·licitant</items></items><items code="at0056"><items id="comment">Equivalent al Filler Order Number a les especificacions HL7 v2.</items><items id="description">L'identificador assignat a l'ordre pel proveïdor sanitari o organització que rep la sol·licitud de servei. També s'anomena identificador d'ordre d'emplenament.</items><items id="text">Identificador d'ordre del receptor</items></items><items code="at0057"><items id="description">Dades sobre el proveïdor o organització sanitària que rep la sol·licitud de servei.</items><items id="text">Receptor</items></items><items code="at0058"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Urgency' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">Urgència del procediment.</items><items id="text">Urgència</items></items><items code="at0060"><items id="comment">Només per al seu ús en associació amb l'etapa "Procediment realitzat", i en situacions en què el procediment es repeteix diverses vegades abans de completar-se, o hi ha diversos components en tot el procediment. Pot ser el mateix que l'atribut de temps RM de l'etapa "Procediment completat".</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the last component of a multicomponent procedure, was finished. (en)</items><items id="text">*End datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0061"><items id="comment">Només per a ús en associació amb l'etapa "Procediment completat".</items><items id="description">Quantitat total de temps emprat a completar el procediment, que pot incloure el temps emprat durant la fase activa del procediment més el temps durant el qual el procediment va estar suspès.</items><items id="text">Durada</items></items><items code="at0062"><items id="description">Representació multimèdia del procediment realitzat.</items><items id="text">Multimèdia</items></items><items code="at0063"><items id="comment">Les ocurrències d'aquest element de dades són il·limitades per permetre escenaris clínics com l'extirpació de múltiples lesions cutànies a diferents llocs, però on tots els altres atributs són idèntics. Utilitzeu aquest element de dades per registrar termes senzills o localitzacions anatòmiques precoordinades. Si els requisits per registrar la localització anatòmica es determinen en temps d'execució per l'aplicació o requereixen un modelatge més complex, com ara localitzacions relatives, utilitzeu CLUSTER.anatomical_location o CLUSTER.relative_location al SLOT "Detalls del procediment" d'aquest arquetip. Si la localització anatòmica s'inclou al “Nom del procediment” mitjançant codis precoordinats, aquest element de dades serà redundant.</items><items id="description">Identificació de la zona del cos per al procediment.</items><items id="text">Zona corporal</items></items><items code="at0064"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">Ampliació</items></items><items code="at0065"><items id="comment">Utilitzeu aquest element de dades per registrar termes senzills o una descripció narrativa. Si els requisits per registrar el mètode requereixen una modelització més complexa, aquesta es pot representar mitjançant arquetips addicionals dins del SLOT "Detall del procediment" d'aquest arquetip. Si el mètode s'inclou al "Nom del procediment" mitjançant codis precoordinats, aquest element de dades serà redundant.</items><items id="description">Identificació del mètode o tècnica específics per al procediment.</items><items id="text">Mètode</items></items><items code="at0066"><items id="comment">Només per utilitzar-lo en associació amb l'etapa "Procediment programat".</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime on which the procedure is intended to be performed. (en)</items><items id="text">*Scheduled datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0067"><items id="comment">Aquest element de dades es pot utilitzar per donar suport a l'organització dins la interfície d'usuari.</items><items id="description">Tipus de procediment.</items><items id="text">Tipus de procediment</items></items><items code="at0068"><items id="description">El procediment o subprocediment en un procediment multicomponent s'ha iniciat.</items><items id="text">Procediment iniciat</items></items><items code="at0069"><items id="comment">Exemples: El pacient estava agitat, buidat insuficient de l'estómac abans de la gastroscòpia, un tumor a les vies biliars impedia el pas de l'endoscopi.</items><items id="description">Dificultats o problemes trobats durant la realització del procediment.</items><items id="text">Dificultats del procediment</items></items><items code="at0070"><items id="comment">*For example: 'Failed bowel preparation' or 'Bowel cancer screening'. Coding of the 'Indication' with a terminology is recommended, if available.  This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required. (en)</items><items id="description">El motiu, clínic o relacionat amb el procés, del procediment.</items><items id="text">Indicació</items></items><items code="at0071"><items id="comment">El mateix procediment, amb la mateixa gravetat o resultat, pot tenir un impacte diferent a cada pacient. Aquest factor de rellevància implica ajustar l'impacte general d'aquest procediment o del seu resultat, segons les característiques del pacient.&#13;
Per exemple: Dos pacients han estat sotmesos al mateix procediment amb el mateix resultat. Reparació mitjançant osteosíntesi de cinquè dit de mà no dominant.&#13;
Un és un jardiner o un peó d'obra; l'altre, un pianista.&#13;
L'impacte d'aquest procediment al pianista és MAJOR (baixa laboral més llarga, necessitat de rehabilitació funcional completa per ajustar a alts requeriments de motricitat fina en activitat laboral).&#13;
Aquest element està destinat a permetre múltiples tipus d'impacte, inclosos però no limitat a: tractament clínic, funcionament a la llar o vida laboral.</items><items id="description">Avaluació de l'impacte o la rellevància d'un procediment o del seu resultat per a un pacient concret.</items><items id="text">Impacte</items></items><items code="at0072"><items id="comment">*For example: An operation with curative intent may be planned, while during the operation it is discovered that curative treatment is not possible and the operation is carried out with a palliative intent instead. Coding of the 'Intent' with a terminology is recommended, if available. This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required. (en)</items><items id="description">*The intended outcome of the procedure. (en)</items><items id="text">*Intent (en)</items></items><items code="at0073"><items id="comment">*For example: the knife to skin time. Only for use in association with the 'Procedure performed', 'Procedure suspended', 'Procedure aborted' or 'Procedure completed' pathway steps. This may be the same as the RM 'time' attribute for the 'Procedure commenced' pathway step. (en)</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the first component of a multicomponent procedure, was first started. (en)</items><items id="text">*Start datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0074"><items id="description">*The duration of time between the start of the most recent pathway step for this procedure and the start of the current pathway step. (en)</items><items id="text">*Pathway step duration (en)</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="de"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Eine klinische Aktivität, die zur Früherkennung, Untersuchung, Diagnose, Heilung, Therapie, Bewertung oder in Hinsicht auf palliative Maßnahmen durchgeführt wird.</items><items id="text">Prozedur</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">Wenn möglich wird die Kodierung der spezifischen Prozedur mit einer Terminologie bevorzugt.</items><items id="description">Identifizierung der Prozedur über den Namen.</items><items id="text">Name der Prozedur</items></items><items code="at0003"><items id="comment">Zur Erfassung detaillierter, strukturierter Informationen über die anatomische Lokalisation, Methode und Technik, verwendetes Equipment, implantierte Geräte, Ergebnisse, Befunde usw.</items><items id="description">Strukturierte Informationen über die Prozedur.</items><items id="text">Details zur Prozedur</items></items><items code="at0004"><items id="description">Die Prozedur, die durchgeführt werden soll, ist geplant.</items><items id="text">Geplante Prozedur</items></items><items code="at0005"><items id="description">Zusätzliche Beschreibung der Aktivität oder der "Pathway"-Verlaufsschritte, die in anderen Bereichen nicht erfasst wurden.</items><items id="text">Kommentar</items></items><items code="at0006"><items id="comment">Verwenden Sie dieses Datenelement, um einfache Begriffe oder präkoordinierte Komplikationen zu erfassen. Wenn die Anforderungen an die Erfassung der Komplikationen komplexer sind, wird die Verwendung eines spezifischen CLUSTER-Archetyps innerhalb des Slots "Details zur Prozedur" in diesem Archetyp empfohlen. Dieses Datenelement wird dann redundant. Beispiele: Hämaturie nach einer Nierenbiopsie, Reizungen des Gewebes nach dem Legen eines intravenösen Katheters.</items><items id="description">Details zu allen Komplikationen, die sich aus der Prozedur ergeben haben.</items><items id="text">Komplikationen</items></items><items code="at0007"><items id="description">Der Auftrag für die Prozedur wurde versendet.</items><items id="text">Auftrag für Prozedur versendet</items></items><items code="at0014"><items id="comment">Zum Beispiel: der Grund für den Abbruch oder die Unterbrechung der Prozedur.</items><items id="description">Grund, warum die angegebene Aktivität für diese Prozedur durchgeführt wurde.</items><items id="text">Grund</items></items><items code="at0034"><items id="comment">(War: Die Prozedur, die durchgeführt werden soll, ist geplant.)</items><items id="description">Dieses Element ist veraltet, da es fälschlicherweise mit dem Status "initial" verknüpft war - verwenden Sie das neue Element "Prozedur geplant" (at0004), das korrekt mit dem Status "geplant" verknüpft ist.</items><items id="text">X - Prozedur geplant</items></items><items code="at0035"><items id="comment">(War: Der Auftrag für die Prozedur wurde versendet.)</items><items id="description">Dieses Element ist veraltet, da es fälschlicherweise mit dem Status "initial" verknüpft war - verwenden Sie das neue Element "Geplante Prozedur" (at0007), das korrekt mit dem Status "geplant" verknüpft ist.</items><items id="text">X - Auftrag für Prozedur versendet</items></items><items code="at0036"><items id="description">Ein Termin für die Prozedur wurde geplant.</items><items id="text">geplanter Termin der Prozedur</items></items><items code="at0038"><items id="description">Die Prozedur wurde verschoben.</items><items id="text">Prozedur verschoben</items></items><items code="at0039"><items id="description">Die geplante Prozedur wurde vor Beginn storniert.</items><items id="text">Prozedur storniert</items></items><items code="at0040"><items id="description">Die Prozedur wurde unterbrochen.</items><items id="text">Prozedur unterbrochen</items></items><items code="at0041"><items id="description">Die Prozedur wurde abgebrochen.</items><items id="text">Prozedur abgebrochen</items></items><items code="at0043"><items id="description">Die Prozedur wurde durchgeführt und alle damit verbundenen klinischen Aktivitäten wurden beendet.</items><items id="text">Prozedur beendet</items></items><items code="at0047"><items id="description">Die Prozedur, oder eine Subprozedur in einem mehrstufigen Vorgehen, wurde durchgeführt.</items><items id="text">Prozedur durchgeführt</items></items><items code="at0048"><items id="comment">Wenn möglich wird die Kodierung mit einer Terminologie bevorzugt.</items><items id="description">Ausgang der durchgeführten Prozedur.</items><items id="text">Ausgang</items></items><items code="at0049"><items id="comment">Zum Beispiel: Beschreibung der Durchführung und der Ergebnisse dieser Prozedur, des abgebrochenen Versuchs oder der Stornierung der Prozedur.</items><items id="description">Beschreibung der Prozedur, angepasst an den "Pathway"-Verlaufsschritt.</items><items id="text">Beschreibung</items></items><items code="at0053"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0054"><items id="comment">Dies entspricht der "Placer Order Number" in den Spezifikationen von HL7 v2.</items><items id="description">Die lokale ID, die dem Auftrag vom Gesundheitsdienstleister oder der Organisation, die die Leistung anfordert, zugewiesen wurde.</items><items id="text">Auftragskennung des Antragstellers</items></items><items code="at0055"><items id="description">Angaben über den Gesundheitsdienstleister oder die Organisation, die die Leistung anfordert.</items><items id="text">Antragsteller</items></items><items code="at0056"><items id="comment">Dies entspricht der "Filler Order Number" in den Spezifikationen von HL7 v2.</items><items id="description">Die ID, die dem Auftrag von dem Gesundheitsdienstleister oder der Organisation, die die Leistungsanforderung erhält, zugewiesen wurde. Dies wird auch als "Filler Order Identifier" bezeichnet.</items><items id="text">Auftragskennung des Empfängers</items></items><items code="at0057"><items id="description">Angaben über den Gesundheitsdienstleister oder die Organisation, die die Leistungsanforderung erhält.</items><items id="text">Empfänger</items></items><items code="at0058"><items id="comment">Wenn möglich wird die Kodierung mit einer Terminologie bevorzugt.</items><items id="description">Dringlichkeit der Prozedur.</items><items id="text">Dringlichkeit</items></items><items code="at0060"><items id="comment">Nur zur Verwendung in Verbindung mit dem Element "Prozedur durchgeführt" und in Situationen, in denen die Prozedur vor dem Abschluss mehrmals wiederholt wird oder die Prozedur sich aus mehreren Komponenten zusammensetzt. Dies kann mit dem RM-Zeitattribut des Elements "Prozedur beendet" übereinstimmen.</items><items id="description">Das Datum und/oder die Uhrzeit, an dem die gesamte Prozedur, oder die letzte Komponente einer mehrstufigen Prozedur, beendet wurde.</items><items id="text">Enddatum/-uhrzeit</items></items><items code="at0061"><items id="comment">Nur in Verbindung mit dem Element "Prozedur beendet" verwenden.</items><items id="description">Die Gesamtdauer der Prozedur - diese kann sich aus der aktiven Phase und der Phase, in der die Prozedur unterbrochen wurde, ergeben.</items><items id="text">Gesamtdauer</items></items><items code="at0062"><items id="description">Multimediale Darstellung der durchgeführten Prozedur.</items><items id="text">Multimedia</items></items><items code="at0063"><items id="comment">Das Vorkommen dieses Datenelements ist nicht eingeschränkt. Dies ermöglicht die Darstellung von klinischen Situationen, in denen alle Eigenschaften, ausgenommen die anatomische Lokalisation, identisch sind, wie z.B. das Entfernen mehrerer Hautläsionen an verschiedenen Stellen. Verwenden Sie dieses Datenelement, um einfache Begriffe oder präkoordinierte anatomische Lokalisationen aufzunehmen. Wenn die Anforderungen an die Erfassung der anatomischen Lokalisation zur Laufzeit durch die Anwendung festgelegt werden oder komplexere Modellierungen wie z.B. die relative Lokalisation erforderlich sind, verwenden Sie entweder CLUSTER.anatomical_location oder CLUSTER.relative_location innerhalb des Slots "Details zur Prozedur" in diesem Archetyp. Wird die anatomische Lokalisation über vordefinierte Codes in den Namen der Prozedur aufgenommen, wird dieses Datenelement redundant.</items><items id="description">Anatomische Lokalisation, an der die Prozedur durchgeführt wird.</items><items id="text">Körperstelle</items></items><items code="at0064"><items id="comment">Zum Beispiel: Lokaler Informationsbedarf oder zusätzliche Metadaten zur Anpassung an FHIR- oder CIMI-Äquivalente.</items><items id="description">Zusätzliche Informationen, die erforderlich sind, um lokale Inhalte zu erfassen oder mit anderen Referenzmodellen/Formalismen abzugleichen.</items><items id="text">Erweiterung</items></items><items code="at0065"><items id="comment">Verwenden Sie dieses Datenelement, um einfache Begriffe oder eine Beschreibung zu erfassen. Wenn die Anforderungen an die Erfassung der Methode eine komplexere Modellierung erfordern, kann dies durch zusätzliche Archetypen innerhalb des SLOTs "Details zur Prozedur" in diesem Archetyp dargestellt werden. Wird die Methode über vordefinierte Codes in dem Element "Name der Prozedur" aufgenommen, wird dieses Datenelement redundant.</items><items id="description">Identifizierung der spezifischen Prozedurmethode oder -technik.</items><items id="text">Methode</items></items><items code="at0066"><items id="comment">Nur für die Verwendung in Verbindung mit dem Element "geplanter Termin der Prozedur" .</items><items id="description">Das Datum und/oder die Uhrzeit für die die Prozedur angesetzt ist.</items><items id="text">Geplantes Datum/Uhrzeit</items></items><items code="at0067"><items id="comment">Dieses pragmatische Datenelement kann zur Unterstützung der Gliederung für die Benutzeroberfläche verwendet werden.</items><items id="description">Die Art der Prozedur.</items><items id="text">Art der Prozedur</items></items><items code="at0068"><items id="description">Die Prozedur, oder eine Subprozedur in einem mehrstufigen Vorgehen, wurde begonnen.</items><items id="text">Prozedur begonnen</items></items><items code="at0069"><items id="comment">Beispiele: Der Patient war unruhig; unzureichende Entleerung des Magens vor der Gastroskopie; ein Tumor in den Gallengängen machte es unmöglich, den Bereich zu passieren.</items><items id="description">Schwierigkeiten oder Probleme, die während der Durchführung der Prozedur aufgetreten sind.</items><items id="text">Schwierigkeiten bei der Durchführung der Prozedur</items></items><items code="at0070"><items id="comment">Die Kodierung der Indikation mit einer Terminologie wird nach Möglichkeit bevorzugt. Dieses Datenelement ermöglicht mehrere Vorkommen. Zum Beispiel: "Fehlgeschlagenen Darmvorbereitung" oder "Darmkrebsvorsorge".</items><items id="description">Der klinische oder prozessbezogene Grund für die Prozedur.</items><items id="text">Indikation</items></items><items code="at0071"><items id="comment">Derselbe Eingriff, bei gleichem Schweregrad oder gleichem Ergebnis, kann sich auf jeden Patienten unterschiedlich auswirken. Dieser Relevanzfaktor beinhaltet die Anpassung der Gesamtauswirkungen des Eingriffs oder des Ergebnisses an die individuellen Merkmale des Patienten.&#13;
&#13;
Beispiel: Zwei Patienten haben sich demselben Eingriff mit gleichem Ergebnis unterzogen: einer Osteosynthese des fünften Fingers ihrer nicht-dominanten Hand.&#13;
&#13;
Einer ist Gärtner oder Bauarbeiter, der andere Pianist.&#13;
&#13;
Die Auswirkungen des Eingriffs sind für den Pianisten GRÖSSER (längere Krankschreibung, Notwendigkeit einer umfassenden funktionellen Rehabilitation zur Anpassung an die hohen feinmotorischen Anforderungen seines Berufs).&#13;
&#13;
Dieses Element soll verschiedene Arten von Auswirkungen berücksichtigen, darunter unter anderem die klinische Behandlung, die Alltagsbewältigung und das Berufsleben.</items><items id="description">Beurteilung der Auswirkungen eines Eingriffs oder seines Ergebnisses für einen bestimmten Patienten.</items><items id="text">Auswirkungen</items></items><items code="at0072"><items id="comment">*For example: An operation with curative intent may be planned, while during the operation it is discovered that curative treatment is not possible and the operation is carried out with a palliative intent instead. Coding of the 'Intent' with a terminology is recommended, if available. This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required.(en)</items><items id="description">*The intended outcome of the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Intent(en)</items></items><items code="at0073"><items id="comment">*For example: the knife to skin time. Only for use in association with the 'Procedure performed', 'Procedure suspended', 'Procedure aborted' or 'Procedure completed' pathway steps. This may be the same as the RM 'time' attribute for the 'Procedure commenced' pathway step.(en)</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the first component of a multicomponent procedure, was first started.(en)</items><items id="text">*Start datetime(en)</items></items><items code="at0074"><items id="description">*The duration of time between the start of the most recent pathway step for this procedure and the start of the current pathway step.(en)</items><items id="text">*Pathway step duration(en)</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="en"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">A clinical activity carried out for screening, investigative, diagnostic, curative, therapeutic, evaluative or palliative purposes.</items><items id="text">Procedure</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">Coding of the 'Procedure name' with a terminology is recommended, if available.</items><items id="description">Identification of the procedure by name.</items><items id="text">Procedure name</items></items><items code="at0003"><items id="comment">Use to capture detailed, structured information about anatomical location, method &amp; technique, equipment used, devices implanted, results, findings etc.</items><items id="description">Structured information about the procedure.</items><items id="text">Procedure detail</items></items><items code="at0004"><items id="description">The procedure to be undertaken is planned.</items><items id="text">Procedure planned</items></items><items code="at0005"><items id="description">Additional narrative about the procedure or care pathway step not captured in other fields.</items><items id="text">Comment</items></items><items code="at0006"><items id="comment">Use this data element to record simple terms or precoordinated complications. For example: Hematuria after a kidney biopsy, tissue irritation after insertion of intravenous catheter. If the requirements for recording complication are more complex then use of a specific CLUSTER archetype within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype is advised and this data element becomes redundant.</items><items id="description">Details about any complication arising from the procedure.</items><items id="text">Complication</items></items><items code="at0007"><items id="description">Request for procedure sent.</items><items id="text">Procedure request sent</items></items><items code="at0014"><items id="comment">For example: the reason for the cancellation or suspension of the procedure.</items><items id="description">Reason that the activity or care pathway step for the identified procedure was carried out.</items><items id="text">Reason</items></items><items code="at0034"><items id="comment">(Was: The procedure to be undertaken is planned.)</items><items id="description">This pathway step has been deprecated as it was incorrectly associated with 'initial' status - use the new 'Procedure planned' (at0004) pathway step  which is correctly associated with 'planned' status.</items><items id="text">X - Procedure planned</items></items><items code="at0035"><items id="comment">(Was: Request for procedure sent.)</items><items id="description">This pathway step has been deprecated as it was incorrectly associated with 'initial' status - use the new 'Procedure request sent' (at0007) pathway step  which is correctly associated with 'planned' status.</items><items id="text">X - Procedure request sent</items></items><items code="at0036"><items id="description">The procedure has been scheduled.</items><items id="text">Procedure scheduled</items></items><items code="at0038"><items id="description">The procedure has been postponed.</items><items id="text">Procedure postponed</items></items><items code="at0039"><items id="description">The planned procedure has been cancelled prior to commencement.</items><items id="text">Procedure cancelled</items></items><items code="at0040"><items id="description">The procedure has been suspended.</items><items id="text">Procedure suspended</items></items><items code="at0041"><items id="description">The procedure has been aborted.</items><items id="text">Procedure aborted</items></items><items code="at0043"><items id="description">The procedure has been performed and all associated clinical activities completed.</items><items id="text">Procedure completed</items></items><items code="at0047"><items id="description">The procedure, or subprocedure in a multicomponent procedure, has been performed.</items><items id="text">Procedure performed</items></items><items code="at0048"><items id="comment">Coding of the 'Outcome' with a terminology is recommended, if available.</items><items id="description">Outcome of procedure performed.</items><items id="text">Outcome</items></items><items code="at0049"><items id="comment">For example: description about the performance and findings from the the procedure, the aborted attempt or the cancellation of the procedure.</items><items id="description">Narrative description about the procedure, as appropriate for the pathway step.</items><items id="text">Description</items></items><items code="at0053"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0054"><items id="comment">This is equivalent to Placer Order Number in HL7 v2 specifications.</items><items id="description">The local ID assigned to the order by the healthcare provider or organisation requesting the service.</items><items id="text">Requestor order identifier</items></items><items code="at0055"><items id="description">Details about the healthcare provider or organisation requesting the service.</items><items id="text">Requestor</items></items><items code="at0056"><items id="comment">This is equivalent to Filler Order Number in HL7 v2 specifications.</items><items id="description">The ID assigned to the order by the healthcare provider or organisation receiving the request for service. This is also referred to as Filler Order Identifier.</items><items id="text">Receiver order identifier</items></items><items code="at0057"><items id="description">Details about the healthcare provider or organisation receiving the request for service.</items><items id="text">Receiver</items></items><items code="at0058"><items id="comment">Coding of the 'Urgency' with a terminology is recommended, if available.</items><items id="description">Urgency of the procedure.</items><items id="text">Urgency</items></items><items code="at0060"><items id="comment">Only for use in association with the 'Procedure performed' pathway step, and in situations where the procedure is repeated on multiple occasions before being completed or there are multiple components to the whole procedure. This may be the same as the RM time attribute for the 'Procedure completed' pathway step.</items><items id="description">The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the last component of a multicomponent procedure, was finished.</items><items id="text">End datetime</items></items><items code="at0061"><items id="comment">Only for use in association with the 'Procedure completed' pathway steps.</items><items id="description">The total amount of time taken to complete the procedure, which may include time spent during the active phase of the procedure plus time during which the procedure was suspended.</items><items id="text">Total duration</items></items><items code="at0062"><items id="description">Mulitimedia representation of a performed procedure.</items><items id="text">Multimedia</items></items><items code="at0063"><items id="comment">Occurrences for this data element are unbounded to allow for clinical scenarios such as removing multiple skin lesions in different places, but where all of the other attributes are identical. Use this data element to record simple terms or precoordinated anatomical locations. If the requirements for recording the anatomical location are determined at run-time by the application or require more complex modelling such as relative locations then use the CLUSTER.anatomical_location or CLUSTER.relative_location within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype. If the anatomical location is included in the 'Procedure name' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant.</items><items id="description">Identification of the body site for the procedure.</items><items id="text">Body site</items></items><items code="at0064"><items id="comment">For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR.</items><items id="description">Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms.</items><items id="text">Extension</items></items><items code="at0065"><items id="comment">Use this data element to record simple terms or a narrative description. If the requirements for recording the method require more complex modelling then this can be represented by additional archetypes within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype. If the method is included in the 'Procedure name' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant.</items><items id="description">Identification of specific method or technique for the procedure.</items><items id="text">Method</items></items><items code="at0066"><items id="comment">Only for use in association with the 'Procedure scheduled' pathway step.</items><items id="description">The date or datetime on which the procedure is intended to be performed.</items><items id="text">Scheduled datetime</items></items><items code="at0067"><items id="comment">This pragmatic data element may be used to support organisation within the user interface.</items><items id="description">The type of procedure.</items><items id="text">Procedure type</items></items><items code="at0068"><items id="description">The procedure, or subprocedure in a multicomponent procedure, has been commenced.</items><items id="text">Procedure commenced</items></items><items code="at0069"><items id="comment">Examples: The patient was agitated, insufficient emptying of the stomach before gastroscopy, a tumour in the bile ducts made it impossible to pass the scope through.</items><items id="description">Difficulties or issues encountered during performance of the procedure.</items><items id="text">Procedural difficulty</items></items><items code="at0070"><items id="comment">For example: 'Failed bowel preparation' or 'Bowel cancer screening'. Coding of the 'Indication' with a terminology is recommended, if available.  This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required.</items><items id="description">The clinical or process-related reason for the procedure.</items><items id="text">Indication</items></items><items code="at0071"><items id="comment">The same procedure, with the same severity or outcome, can have a different impact on each patient. This relevance factor involves adjusting the overall impact of that procedure or outcome according to the patient's characteristics.&#13;
&#13;
For example: Two patients have undergone the same procedure with the same outcome: osteosynthesis repair of the fifth finger of their non-dominant hand.&#13;
&#13;
One is a gardener or construction worker; the other, a pianist.&#13;
&#13;
The impact of that procedure on the pianist is GREATER (longer sick leave, need for full functional rehabilitation to adapt to the high fine motor demands of work).&#13;
&#13;
This element is intended to allow for multiple types of impact, including but not limited to: clinical treatment, home functioning, or work life.</items><items id="description">Assessment of the impact of a procedure or its outcome for a specific patient.</items><items id="text">Impact</items></items><items code="at0072"><items id="comment">For example: An operation with curative intent may be planned, while during the operation it is discovered that curative treatment is not possible and the operation is carried out with a palliative intent instead. Coding of the 'Intent' with a terminology is recommended, if available. This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required.</items><items id="description">The intended outcome of the procedure.</items><items id="text">Intent</items></items><items code="at0073"><items id="comment">For example: the knife to skin time. Only for use in association with the 'Procedure performed', 'Procedure suspended', 'Procedure aborted' or 'Procedure completed' pathway steps. This may be the same as the RM 'time' attribute for the 'Procedure commenced' pathway step.</items><items id="description">The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the first component of a multicomponent procedure, was first started.</items><items id="text">Start datetime</items></items><items code="at0074"><items id="description">The duration of time between the start of the most recent pathway step for this procedure and the start of the current pathway step.</items><items id="text">Pathway step duration</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="es"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Actividad clínica llevada a cabo con fines de cribado, investigación, diagnóstico, curativos, terapéuticos, de evaluación o paliativos.</items><items id="text">Procedimiento</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Procedure name' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">Identificación del procedimiento por su nombre.</items><items id="text">Nombre del procedimiento</items></items><items code="at0003"><items id="comment">Se utiliza para recopilar información detallada y estructurada sobre la localización anatómica, el método y la técnica, el equipo utilizado, los dispositivos implantados, los resultados, los hallazgos, etc.</items><items id="description">Información estructurada sobre el procedimiento.</items><items id="text">Detalles del procedimiento</items></items><items code="at0004"><items id="description">Se planifica el procedimiento a llevar a cabo.</items><items id="text">Procedimiento planificado</items></items><items code="at0005"><items id="description">*Additional narrative about the procedure or care pathway step not captured in other fields. (en)</items><items id="text">Comentarios</items></items><items code="at0006"><items id="comment">*Use this data element to record simple terms or precoordinated complications. For example: Hematuria after a kidney biopsy, tissue irritation after insertion of intravenous catheter. If the requirements for recording complication are more complex then use of a specific CLUSTER archetype within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype is advised and this data element becomes redundant. (en)</items><items id="description">Detalles sobre cualquier complicación derivada del procedimiento.</items><items id="text">Complicación</items></items><items code="at0007"><items id="description">Solicitud de procedimiento enviada.</items><items id="text">Solicitud de procedimiento enviada</items></items><items code="at0014"><items id="comment">Por ejemplo: motivo de la cancelación o suspensión del procedimiento.</items><items id="description">Motivo por el que se llevó a cabo la actividad o etapa asistencial para el procedimiento identificado.</items><items id="text">Motivo</items></items><items code="at0034"><items id="comment">(Obsoleto: Se planifica el procedimiento a llevar a cabo.)</items><items id="description">Este apartado ha quedado obsoleto, ya que se asociaba incorrectamente con el estado "inicial". Utilice el nuevo apartado "Procedimiento planificado" (at0004), asociado correctamente con el estado "planificado".</items><items id="text">X - Procedimiento planificado</items></items><items code="at0035"><items id="comment">(Obsoleto: Solicitud de procedimiento enviada.)</items><items id="description">Este apartado ha quedado obsoleto, ya que se asociaba incorrectamente con el estado "inicial". Utilice el nuevo apartado "Solicitud de procedimiento enviada" (at0004), asociado correctamente con el estado "planificado".</items><items id="text">X - Solicitud de procedimiento enviada</items></items><items code="at0036"><items id="description">Se ha programado el procedimiento.</items><items id="text">Procedimiento programado</items></items><items code="at0038"><items id="description">El procedimiento se ha pospuesto.</items><items id="text">Procedimiento pospuesto</items></items><items code="at0039"><items id="description">El procedimiento previsto se ha cancelado antes de comenzar.</items><items id="text">Procedimiento cancelado</items></items><items code="at0040"><items id="description">Se ha suspendido el procedimiento.</items><items id="text">Procedimiento suspendido</items></items><items code="at0041"><items id="description">Se ha interrumpido el procedimiento.</items><items id="text">Procedimiento interrumpido</items></items><items code="at0043"><items id="description">Se ha realizado el procedimiento y se han completado todas las actividades clínicas asociadas.</items><items id="text">Procedimiento completado</items></items><items code="at0047"><items id="description">El procedimiento, o subprocedimiento en un procedimiento multicomponente, se ha realizado.</items><items id="text">Procedimiento realizado</items></items><items code="at0048"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Outcome' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">Resultado del procedimiento realizado.</items><items id="text">Resultado</items></items><items code="at0049"><items id="comment">Por ejemplo: descripción de la realización y los resultados del procedimiento, el intento interrumpido o la cancelación del procedimiento.</items><items id="description">Descripción narrativa sobre el procedimiento, según corresponda a la fase del proceso.</items><items id="text">Descripción</items></items><items code="at0053"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0054"><items id="comment">Equivalente al Placer Order Number en las especificaciones HL7 v2.</items><items id="description">El ID local asignado a la orden por el proveedor sanitario o la organización que solicita el servicio.</items><items id="text">Identificador de orden del solicitante</items></items><items code="at0055"><items id="description">Datos del profesional sanitario u organización que solicita el servicio.</items><items id="text">Solicitante</items></items><items code="at0056"><items id="comment">Equivalente al Placer Order Number en las especificaciones HL7 v2.</items><items id="description">El identificador asignado a la orden por el proveedor sanitario o la organización que recibe la solicitud de servicio. También se denomina Identificador de Orden de Cumplimentación.</items><items id="text">Identificador de orden del receptor</items></items><items code="at0057"><items id="description">Datos sobre el proveedor u organización sanitaria que recibe la solicitud de servicio.</items><items id="text">Receptor</items></items><items code="at0058"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Urgency' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">Urgencia del procedimiento.</items><items id="text">Urgencia</items></items><items code="at0060"><items id="comment">Sólo para su uso en asociación con la etapa "Procedimiento realizado", y en situaciones en las que el procedimiento se repite en varias ocasiones antes de completarse, o hay varios componentes en todo el procedimiento. Puede ser el mismo que el atributo de tiempo RM de la etapa "Procedimiento completado".</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the last component of a multicomponent procedure, was finished. (en)</items><items id="text">*End datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0061"><items id="comment">Sólo para su uso en asociación con la etapa "Procedimiento completado".</items><items id="description">Cantidad total de tiempo empleado en completar el procedimiento, que puede incluir el tiempo empleado durante la fase activa del procedimiento más el tiempo durante el cual el procedimiento estuvo suspendido.</items><items id="text">Duración</items></items><items code="at0062"><items id="description">Representación multimedia del procedimiento realizado.</items><items id="text">Multimedia</items></items><items code="at0063"><items id="comment">Las ocurrencias de este elemento de datos son ilimitadas para permitir escenarios clínicos como la extirpación de múltiples lesiones cutáneas en diferentes lugares, pero donde todos los demás atributos son idénticos. Utilice este elemento de datos para registrar términos sencillos o localizaciones anatómicas precoordinadas. Si los requisitos para registrar la localización anatómica se determinan en tiempo de ejecución por la aplicación o requieren un modelado más complejo, como localizaciones relativas, utilice CLUSTER.anatomical_location o CLUSTER.relative_location en el SLOT "Detalles del procedimiento" de este arquetipo. Si la localización anatómica se incluye en el "Nombre del procedimiento" mediante códigos precoordinados, este elemento de datos será redundante.</items><items id="description">Identificación de la zona del cuerpo para el procedimiento.</items><items id="text">Zona corporal</items></items><items code="at0064"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">Ampliación</items></items><items code="at0065"><items id="comment">Utilice este elemento de datos para registrar términos sencillos o una descripción narrativa. Si los requisitos para registrar el método requieren una modelización más compleja, ésta puede representarse mediante arquetipos adicionales dentro del SLOT "Detalle del procedimiento", de este arquetipo. Si el método se incluye en el "Nombre del procedimiento" mediante códigos precoordinados, este elemento de datos será redundante.</items><items id="description">Identificación del método o técnica específicos para el procedimiento.</items><items id="text">Método</items></items><items code="at0066"><items id="comment">Sólo para su uso en asociación con la etapa "Procedimiento programado".</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime on which the procedure is intended to be performed. (en)</items><items id="text">*Scheduled datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0067"><items id="comment">Este elemento de datos puede utilizarse para dar soporte a la organización dentro de la interfaz de usuario.</items><items id="description">Tipo de procedimiento.</items><items id="text">Tipo de procedimiento</items></items><items code="at0068"><items id="description">El procedimiento, o subprocedimiento en un procedimiento multicomponente, se ha iniciado.</items><items id="text">Procedimiento iniciado</items></items><items code="at0069"><items id="comment">Ejemplos: El paciente estaba agitado, vaciado insuficiente del estómago antes de la gastroscopia, un tumor en las vías biliares impedía el paso del endoscopio.</items><items id="description">Dificultades o problemas encontrados durante la realización del procedimiento.</items><items id="text">Dificultades del procedimiento</items></items><items code="at0070"><items id="comment">*For example: 'Failed bowel preparation' or 'Bowel cancer screening'. Coding of the 'Indication' with a terminology is recommended, if available.  This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required. (en)</items><items id="description">El motivo, clínico o relacionado con el proceso, del procedimiento.</items><items id="text">Indicación</items></items><items code="at0071"><items id="comment">El mismo procedimiento, con la misma gravedad o resultado, puede tener un impacto diferente en cada paciente. Este factor de relevancia implica ajustar el impacto general de ese procedimiento o de su resultado, según las características del paciente.&#13;
Por ejemplo: Dos pacientes se han sometido al mismo procedimiento con el mismo resultado. Reparación mediante osteosíntesis de quinto dedo de mano no dominante. &#13;
&#13;
Uno es una jardinero o un peon de obra; el otro, un pianista.&#13;
El impacto de ese procedimiento en el pianista es MAYOR (baja laboral mas larga, necesidad de rehabilitación funcional completa para ajustar a altos requerimientos de motricidad fina en actividad laboral ).&#13;
Este elemento está destinado a permitir múltiples tipos de impacto, incluidos pero no limitado a: tratamiento clínico, funcionamiento en el hogar o vida laboral.</items><items id="description">Evaluación global del impacto o relevancia de un procedimiento o su resultado para un paciente concreto.</items><items id="text">Impacto</items></items><items code="at0072"><items id="comment">*For example: An operation with curative intent may be planned, while during the operation it is discovered that curative treatment is not possible and the operation is carried out with a palliative intent instead. Coding of the 'Intent' with a terminology is recommended, if available. This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required. (en)</items><items id="description">*The intended outcome of the procedure. (en)</items><items id="text">*Intent (en)</items></items><items code="at0073"><items id="comment">*For example: the knife to skin time. Only for use in association with the 'Procedure performed', 'Procedure suspended', 'Procedure aborted' or 'Procedure completed' pathway steps. This may be the same as the RM 'time' attribute for the 'Procedure commenced' pathway step. (en)</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the first component of a multicomponent procedure, was first started. (en)</items><items id="text">*Start datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0074"><items id="description">*The duration of time between the start of the most recent pathway step for this procedure and the start of the current pathway step. (en)</items><items id="text">*Pathway step duration (en)</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="nb"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">En klinisk aktivitet som er utført i undersøkende, diagnostisk, kurativ, terapeutisk, evaluerende, prognostisk eller palliativ hensikt.</items><items id="text">Prosedyre</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">Det anbefales å kode "Prosedyrenavn" med en terminologi, om mulig.</items><items id="description">Navnet på prosedyren.</items><items id="text">Prosedyrenavn</items></items><items code="at0003"><items id="comment">Bruk for å registrere detaljert, strukturert informasjon om anatomisk lokalisering, metode og teknikker, utstyr som ble benyttet, medisinsk utstyr som ble implantert, funn, etc.</items><items id="description">Strukturert informasjon om prosedyren.</items><items id="text">Prosedyredetaljer</items></items><items code="at0004"><items id="description">Prosedyren er planlagt.</items><items id="text">Prosedyre planlagt</items></items><items code="at0005"><items id="description">Ytterligere fritekst om prosedyren eller prosesstrinnet som ikke er registrert i andre felt.</items><items id="text">Kommentar</items></items><items code="at0006"><items id="comment">Bruk dette dataelementet til å registrere enkle termer eller prekoordinerte komplikasjoner. For eksempel hematuri etter nyrebiopsi eller vevsirritasjon etter innlegging av intravenøst kateter. Dersom kravene til registrering av komplikasjoner er mer komplekse, anbefales bruk av en spesifikk CLUSTER‑arketype i "Prosedyredetaljer"-SLOTet i denne arketypen, og dette dataelementet blir da overflødig.</items><items id="description">Detaljer om komplikasjoner oppstått under gjennomføring av prosedyren.</items><items id="text">Komplikasjon</items></items><items code="at0007"><items id="description">Det er sendt rekvisisjon for prosedyren.</items><items id="text">Prosedyrerekvisisjon sendt</items></items><items code="at0014"><items id="comment">For eksempel grunnen til at prosedyren ble avlyst eller midlertidig stanset.</items><items id="description">Begrunnelse for at aktiviteten eller prosesstrinnet for den aktuelle prosedyren ble utført.</items><items id="text">Begrunnelse</items></items><items code="at0034"><items id="comment">(Var: Prosedyren er planlagt.)</items><items id="description">Dette prosesstrinnet er satt ut av bruk, siden det ved en feil hadde statusen "initial". Bruk det nye prosesstrinnet "Prosedyre planlagt" (at0004) som har den korrekte statusen "planned".</items><items id="text">X - Prosedyre planlagt</items></items><items code="at0035"><items id="comment">(Var: Det er sendt rekvisisjon for prosedyren.)</items><items id="description">Dette prosesstrinnet er satt ut av bruk, siden det ved en feil hadde statusen "initial". Bruk det nye prosesstrinnet "Prosedyre planlagt" (at0007) som har den korrekte statusen "planned".</items><items id="text">X - Prosedyrerekvisisjon sendt</items></items><items code="at0036"><items id="description">Tidspunkt for prosedyre er fastsatt.</items><items id="text">Fastsatt tidspunkt for prosedyre</items></items><items code="at0038"><items id="description">Prosedyren er utsatt.</items><items id="text">Prosedyre utsatt</items></items><items code="at0039"><items id="description">Den planlagte prosedyren har blitt avlyst før den ble igangsatt.</items><items id="text">Prosedyre avlyst</items></items><items code="at0040"><items id="description">Prosedyren er suspendert/ midlertidig stanset.</items><items id="text">Prosedyre midlertidig stanset</items></items><items code="at0041"><items id="description">Prosedyren har blitt avbrutt.</items><items id="text">Prosedyre avbrutt</items></items><items code="at0043"><items id="description">Prosedyren er utført og alle tilknyttede kliniske handlinger er fullførte.</items><items id="text">Prosedyre fullført</items></items><items code="at0047"><items id="description">Prosedyren eller en del av en prosedyre som består av flere delprosedyrer er utført.</items><items id="text">Prosedyre utført</items></items><items code="at0048"><items id="comment">Det anbefales å kode "Resultat" med en terminologi, om mulig.</items><items id="description">Resultatet av den utførte prosedyren.</items><items id="text">Resultat</items></items><items code="at0049"><items id="comment">For eksempel en beskrivelse av utførelsen og funnene fra prosedyren, det avbrutte forsøket, eller avlysningen av prosedyren.</items><items id="description">Fritekstbeskrivelse av prosedyren, tilpasset det aktuelle prosesstrinnet.</items><items id="text">Beskrivelse</items></items><items code="at0053"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0054"><items id="comment">Tilsvarer "Placer Order Number" i HL7 v2-spesifikasjonene.</items><items id="description">Den lokale IDen tilordnet rekvisisjonen av helsepersonellet eller organisasjonen som rekvirerer prosedyren.</items><items id="text">Rekvisisjonsidentifikator</items></items><items code="at0055"><items id="description">Detaljer om helsepersonellet eller organisasjonen som har rekvirert prosedyren.</items><items id="text">Rekvirent</items></items><items code="at0056"><items id="comment">Tilsvarer "Filler Order Number" i HL7 v2-spesifikasjonene.</items><items id="description">IDen tilordnet rekvisisjonen av helsepersonellet eller organisasjonen som mottar rekvisisjonen.</items><items id="text">Mottakers rekvisisjonsidentifikator</items></items><items code="at0057"><items id="description">Detaljer om helsepersonellet eller organisasjonen som mottar prosedyrerekvisisjonen.</items><items id="text">Mottaker</items></items><items code="at0058"><items id="comment">Det anbefales å kode "Hastegrad" med en terminologi, om mulig.</items><items id="description">Prosedyrens hastegrad.</items><items id="text">Hastegrad</items></items><items code="at0060"><items id="comment">Kun for bruk i forbindelse med prosesstrinnet "Prosedyre utført" og i situasjoner der prosedyren gjentas flere ganger før den fullføres, eller det finnes flere komponenter i prosedyren. Dette kan være det samme som RM-attributtet "time" for prosesstrinnet "Prosedyre utført".</items><items id="description">Dato eller datotid da hele prosedyren, eller den siste komponenten i en flerkomponentprosedyre, ble avsluttet.</items><items id="text">Slutt datotid</items></items><items code="at0061"><items id="comment">Kun for bruk i forbindelse med prosesstrinnet "Prosedyre fullført".</items><items id="description">Den totale tiden som ble brukt til å fullføre prosedyren. Dette kan omfatte tidsbruk under den aktive fasen av prosedyren, og i tillegg tid da prosedyren var midlertidig stanset.</items><items id="text">Total varighet</items></items><items code="at0062"><items id="description">Multimediarepresentasjon av en utført prosedyre.</items><items id="text">Multimedia</items></items><items code="at0063"><items id="comment">Forekomster for dette dataelementet er satt ubegrenset for å tillate kliniske scenarier som f.eks. å fjerne flere hudlesjoner på forskjellige steder, men der alle de andre attributtene er identiske. Bruk dette dataelementet til å registrere enkle termer eller prekoordinerte anatomiske lokaliseringer. Dersom behovene for registrering av anatomisk lokalisering bestemmes først av applikasjonen eller krever mer kompleks modellering som f.eks. relative lokaliseringer, kan arketypene CLUSTER.anatomical_location eller CLUSTER.relative_location brukes i SLOTet "Prosedyredetaljer" i denne arketypen. Dersom den anatomiske lokaliseringen inkluderes som en del av "Prosedyrenavn"-elementet ved hjelp av prekoordinerte koder blir dette dataelementet overflødig.</items><items id="description">Stedet på kroppen der prosedyren er utført.</items><items id="text">Kroppssted</items></items><items code="at0064"><items id="comment">For eksempel lokale informasjonsbehov eller ytterligere metadata for å kunne tilpasse til tilsvarende konsepter i FHIR.</items><items id="description">Ytterligere informasjon som trengs for å kunne registrere lokalt definert innhold eller for å tilpasse til andre referansemodeller eller formalismer.</items><items id="text">Tilleggsinformasjon</items></items><items code="at0065"><items id="comment">Bruk dette dataelementet til å registrere enkle termer eller en fritekstlig beskrivelse. Dersom behovene for beskrivelse av metoden krever mer kompleks modellering, kan dette representeres ved hjelp av tilleggsarketyper i SLOTet "Prosedyredetaljer" i denne arketypen. Dersom metoden inkluderes som en del av "Prosedyrenavn"-elementet ved hjelp av prekoordinerte koder blir dette dataelementet overflødig.</items><items id="description">Den spesifikke metoden eller teknikken for prosedyren.</items><items id="text">Metode</items></items><items code="at0066"><items id="comment">Kun til bruk i forbindelse med prosesstrinnet "Fastsatt tidspunkt for prosedyre".</items><items id="description">Dato eller datotid for når prosedyren er planlagt utført.</items><items id="text">Planlagt datotid</items></items><items code="at0067"><items id="comment">Dette dataelementet kan brukes til å støtte organisering innenfor brukergrensesnittet.</items><items id="description">Typen prosedyre.</items><items id="text">Prosedyretype</items></items><items code="at0068"><items id="description">Prosedyren eller en del av en prosedyre som består av flere delprosedyrer er påbegynt.</items><items id="text">Prosedyre påbegynt</items></items><items code="at0069"><items id="comment">Eksempler: Pasienten var urolig, magen var ikke skikkelig tømt før gastroskopi, en svulst i gallegangene gjorde det umulig å få skopet gjennom.</items><items id="description">Vanskeligheter eller problemer som det ble støtt på under prosedyren.</items><items id="text">Problem ved prosedyre</items></items><items code="at0070"><items id="comment">For eksempel "Mislykket tarmtømming" eller "Tarmkreftscreening". Det anbefales å kode "Indikasjon" med en terminologi, om mulig. Dette dataelementet tillater flere forekomster, for å tillate brukeren å registrere flere svar ved behov.</items><items id="description">Den kliniske eller prosessrelaterte årsaken til prosedyren.</items><items id="text">Indikasjon</items></items><items code="at0071"><items id="comment">Samme prosedyre, med samme alvorlighetsgrad eller utfall, kan ha ulik konsekvens for hver enkelt pasient. Denne relevansfaktoren innebærer å justere den samlede påvirkningen av prosedyren eller utfallet i henhold til pasientens individuelle kjennetegn.&#13;
&#13;
For eksempel: To pasienter har gjennomgått samme prosedyre med samme resultat: osteosyntese av femte finger på ikke-dominant hånd.&#13;
&#13;
Den ene er gartner eller bygningsarbeider, den andre er pianist.&#13;
&#13;
Inngrepets konsekvens for pianisten er STØRRE (lengre sykmelding, behov for full funksjonell rehabilitering for å tilpasse seg de høye kravene til finmotorikk i arbeidet).&#13;
&#13;
Dette elementet er ment å ta høyde for flere typer konsekvenser, inkludert klinisk behandling, funksjon i hjemmet og arbeidsliv.</items><items id="description">Vurdering av prosedyrens konsekvens eller resultat for individet.</items><items id="text">Konsekvens</items></items><items code="at0072"><items id="comment">For eksempel kan en operasjon planlegges med kurativ hensikt, men under operasjonen blir det oppdaget at kurativ behandling ikke er mulig, og operasjonen utføres med palliativ hensikt i stedet. Det anbefales å kode "Hensikt" med en terminologi, om mulig. Dette dataelementet tillater flere forekomster, for å tillate brukeren å registrere flere svar ved behov.</items><items id="description">Det ønskede resultatet av prosedyren.</items><items id="text">Hensikt</items></items><items code="at0073"><items id="comment">For eksempel tidspunktet for første snitt. Kun til bruk i sammenheng med prosesstrinnene "Prosedyre utført", "Prosedyre midlertidig stanset", "Prosedyre avbrutt" eller "Prosedyre fullført". Dette kan være det samme som RM-attributtet "time" for prosesstrinnet "Prosedyre påbegynt".</items><items id="description">Dato eller datotid da hele prosedyren, eller den første komponenten i en flerkomponentprosedyre, først ble startet.</items><items id="text">Start datotid</items></items><items code="at0074"><items id="description">Tidsrommet mellom starten på det forrige prosesstrinnet for denne prosedyren og starten på gjeldende prosesstrinn.</items><items id="text">Varighet av prosesstrinn</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="pt-br"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">A atividade clínica realizada para rastreamento , investigação , diagnóstico , cura , terapêutica, avaliação ou finalidade paliativos.</items><items id="text">Procedimento</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Procedure name' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">Identificação do procedimento pelo nome.</items><items id="text">Nome do procedimento</items></items><items code="at0003"><items id="comment">Use para capturar informações detalhadas , estruturadas sobre a localização anatômica , método e técnica , os equipamentos utilizados , dispositivos implantados , os resultados , as conclusões, etc.</items><items id="description">São as informações estruturadas sobre o procedimento.</items><items id="text">Detalhes do Procedimento</items></items><items code="at0004"><items id="description">*</items><items id="text">*Procedure planned (en)</items></items><items code="at0005"><items id="description">*Additional narrative about the procedure or care pathway step not captured in other fields. (en)</items><items id="text">Comentários</items></items><items code="at0006"><items id="comment">*Use this data element to record simple terms or precoordinated complications. For example: Hematuria after a kidney biopsy, tissue irritation after insertion of intravenous catheter. If the requirements for recording complication are more complex then use of a specific CLUSTER archetype within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype is advised and this data element becomes redundant. (en)</items><items id="description">Detalhes sobre alguma complicação decorrente do procedimento</items><items id="text">Complicações</items></items><items code="at0007"><items id="description">*</items><items id="text">*Procedure request sent (en)</items></items><items code="at0014"><items id="comment">Por exemplo: o motivo do cancelamento ou suspensão de um procedimento.</items><items id="description">Razão pela qual a atividade ou cuidado foi identificada para que o procedimento fosse realizado.</items><items id="text">Justificativa</items></items><items code="at0034"><items id="description">O procedimento a ser realizado é planejado</items><items id="text">Plano de procedimento</items></items><items code="at0035"><items id="description">Pedido de procedimento enviado.</items><items id="text">Procedimento pedido enviado</items></items><items code="at0036"><items id="description">O procedimento foi agendado.</items><items id="text">Procedimento agendado</items></items><items code="at0038"><items id="description">O procedimento foi adiado.</items><items id="text">Procedimento adiado</items></items><items code="at0039"><items id="description">O procedimento planejado foi cancelado antes do início.</items><items id="text">Procedimento cancelado</items></items><items code="at0040"><items id="description">O procedimento foi suspenso.</items><items id="text">Procedimento suspenso</items></items><items code="at0041"><items id="description">O procedimento foi abortado.</items><items id="text">Procedimento abortado</items></items><items code="at0043"><items id="description">O procedimento foi realizado e todas as atividades clínicas associadas concluídas.</items><items id="text">Procedimento concluído</items></items><items code="at0047"><items id="description">O procedimento, ou procedimento secundário no caso de procedimentos sequenciado, foi realizado.</items><items id="text">Procedimento realizado</items></items><items code="at0048"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Outcome' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">Resultado do procedimento realizado.</items><items id="text">Resultado</items></items><items code="at0049"><items id="comment">Por exemplo : Descrição sobre o desempenho e os resultados do procedimento, a tentativa abortada ou a anulação do procedimento.</items><items id="description">Descrição narrativa sobre o procedimento, conforme apropriado para a etapa.</items><items id="text">Descrição</items></items><items code="at0053"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree(en)</items></items><items code="at0054"><items id="comment">Isto é equivalente ao "Placer Order Number" nas especificações do HL7 v2.</items><items id="description">O ID local atribuído ao pedido realizado pelo profissional de saúde ou organização solicitando o serviço.</items><items id="text">Identificador do pedido do solicitante</items></items><items code="at0055"><items id="description">Detalhes sobre o profissional ou organização de saúde que solicitou o serviço.</items><items id="text">Solicitante</items></items><items code="at0056"><items id="comment">Isto é equivalente ao "Placer Order Number" nas especificações do HL7 v2.</items><items id="description">O ID atribuído ao pedido pelo provedor de cuidados de saúde ou organização que recebe o pedido de serviço. Isto é também relacionado ao preenchimento da identificação do pedido.</items><items id="text">Identificador do pedido do destinatário</items></items><items code="at0057"><items id="description">Detalhes sobre o profissional ou organização de saúde que recebeu o requerimento para o serviço.</items><items id="text">Destinatário</items></items><items code="at0058"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Urgency' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">Urgência do procedimento.</items><items id="text">Urgência</items></items><items code="at0060"><items id="comment">Apenas para utilização em associação com o "Procedimento realizado" da etapa, e em situações em que o procedimento é repetido em várias ocasiões antes de ser concluído ou houver vários componentes para todo o processo. Este pode ser o mesmo que o atributo para o tempo de RM "Processo concluído".</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the last component of a multicomponent procedure, was finished. (en)</items><items id="text">*End datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0061"><items id="comment">Apenas para utilização em associação com o "Procedimento concluído".</items><items id="description">A quantidade total de tempo necessária para concluir o procedimento, o que pode incluir o tempo gasto durante a fase ativa do procedimento mais o tempo durante o qual o procedimento foi suspenso.</items><items id="text">Duração Total</items></items><items code="at0062"><items id="description">Representação multimídia de um procedimento realizado.</items><items id="text">Multimidia</items></items><items code="at0063"><items id="comment">Ocorrências para este elemento de dados são ilimitadas para permitir cenários clínicos, tais como a remoção de lesões da pele em múltiplos locais diferentes , mas em que todos os outros atributos são idênticos . Utilize este elemento de dados para gravar termos simples ou localizações anatômicas padrão. Se as condições de gravação da localização anatômica são determinados em tempo de execução pelo aplicativo ou exigir modelagem mais complexa, como localizações relativas , em seguida, usar o CLUSTER.anatomical_location ou CLUSTER.relative_location dentro do campo "detalhes do procedimento" neste arquétipo. Se a localização anatômica estiver incluída no "Nome do procedimento" através de códigos padronizados, este elemento de dados torna-se redundante.</items><items id="description">Identificação do local no corpo onde será realizado o procedimento.</items><items id="text">Localização no corpo</items></items><items code="at0064"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">Extensão</items></items><items code="at0065"><items id="comment">Utilize este elemento de dados para registrar termos simples ou uma descrição narrativa . Se as condições de registro do método requer uma modelagem mais complexa , então isso pode ser representado por arquétipos adicionais dentro do campo "Detalhes do procedimento" deste arquétipo. Se o método está incluído no "Nome do procedimento" através de códigos padrão , este elemento de dados torna-se redundante.</items><items id="description">Identificação do método específico ou técnica do procedimento.</items><items id="text">Método</items></items><items code="at0066"><items id="comment">Apenas para utilização em associação com o " Procedimento Programado ' para a etapa em curso.</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime on which the procedure is intended to be performed. (en)</items><items id="text">*Scheduled datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0067"><items id="comment">Esse elemento de dados pragmático pode ser usado para apoiar a organização dentro da interface do usuário.</items><items id="description">O tipo do procedimento.</items><items id="text">Tipo do procedimento</items></items><items code="at0068"><items id="description">O procedimento, ou procedimento secundário, no caso de procedimentos sequenciados, foi iniciado.</items><items id="text">Procedimento Iniciou</items></items><items code="at0069"><items id="description">*Difficulties or issues encountered during the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedural difficulty(en)</items></items><items code="at0070"><items id="comment">*For example: 'Failed bowel preparation' or 'Bowel cancer screening'. Coding of the 'Indication' with a terminology is recommended, if available.  This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required. (en)</items><items id="description">*The clinical or process-related reason for the procedure. (en)</items><items id="text">*Indication (en)</items></items><items code="at0071"><items id="description"/><items id="text">*DV_TEXT (en)</items></items><items code="at0072"><items id="comment">*For example: An operation with curative intent may be planned, while during the operation it is discovered that curative treatment is not possible and the operation is carried out with a palliative intent instead. Coding of the 'Intent' with a terminology is recommended, if available. This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required. (en)</items><items id="description">*The intended outcome of the procedure. (en)</items><items id="text">*Intent (en)</items></items><items code="at0073"><items id="comment">*For example: the knife to skin time. Only for use in association with the 'Procedure performed', 'Procedure suspended', 'Procedure aborted' or 'Procedure completed' pathway steps. This may be the same as the RM 'time' attribute for the 'Procedure commenced' pathway step. (en)</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the first component of a multicomponent procedure, was first started. (en)</items><items id="text">*Start datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0074"><items id="description">*The duration of time between the start of the most recent pathway step for this procedure and the start of the current pathway step. (en)</items><items id="text">*Pathway step duration (en)</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="pt-pt"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">Atividade clínica realizada para fins de rastreio, investigação, diagnóstico, cura, tratamento, avaliação ou cuidados paliativos.</items><items id="text">Procedimento</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Procedure name' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">Identificação do procedimento pelo nome.</items><items id="text">Nome do procedimento</items></items><items code="at0003"><items id="comment">Use para capturar informações detalhadas e estruturadas sobre localização anatómica, método e técnica, equipamentos usados, dispositivos implantados, resultados, descobertas, etc.</items><items id="description">Informação estruturada sobre o procedimento.</items><items id="text">Detalhe do procedimento</items></items><items code="at0004"><items id="description">O procedimento a ser realizado está planeado.</items><items id="text">Procedimento Planeado</items></items><items code="at0005"><items id="description">*Additional narrative about the procedure or care pathway step not captured in other fields. (en)</items><items id="text">Comentário</items></items><items code="at0006"><items id="comment">*Use this data element to record simple terms or precoordinated complications. For example: Hematuria after a kidney biopsy, tissue irritation after insertion of intravenous catheter. If the requirements for recording complication are more complex then use of a specific CLUSTER archetype within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype is advised and this data element becomes redundant. (en)</items><items id="description">Detalhes sobre qualquer complicação decorrente do procedimento.</items><items id="text">Complicação</items></items><items code="at0007"><items id="description">Pedido para o procedimento enviado.</items><items id="text">Pedido de procedimento enviado</items></items><items code="at0014"><items id="comment">Por exemplo: o motivo do cancelamento ou suspensão do procedimento.</items><items id="description">Motivo pelo qual foi realizada a etapa da atividade ou da via de cuidado para o procedimento identificado.</items><items id="text">Motivo</items></items><items code="at0034"><items id="comment">(Era: O procedimento a ser realizado está planeado.)</items><items id="description">Esta etapa de caminho foi preterida, pois foi incorretamente associada ao estado 'inicial' - use a nova etapa de caminho 'Procedimento planeado' (at0004) que está corretamente associada ao estado 'planeado'.</items><items id="text">X - Procedimento planeado</items></items><items code="at0035"><items id="comment">(Foi: Pedido de procedimento enviado.)</items><items id="description">Esta etapa de caminho foi preterida, pois foi incorretamente associada ao estado 'inicial' - use a nova etapa de caminho 'Pedido de procedimento enviado' (at0007) que está corretamente associada ao estado 'planeado'.</items><items id="text">X - Solicitação de procedimento enviada</items></items><items code="at0036"><items id="description">O procedimento foi agendado.</items><items id="text">Procedimento programado</items></items><items code="at0038"><items id="description">O procedimento foi adiado.</items><items id="text">Procedimento Adiado</items></items><items code="at0039"><items id="description">O procedimento previsto foi cancelado antes do início.</items><items id="text">Procedimento Cancelado</items></items><items code="at0040"><items id="description">O procedimento foi suspenso.</items><items id="text">Procedimento suspenso</items></items><items code="at0041"><items id="description">O procedimento foi abortado.</items><items id="text">Procedimento abortado</items></items><items code="at0043"><items id="description">O procedimento foi realizado e todas as atividades clínicas associadas foram concluídas.</items><items id="text">Procedimento concluído</items></items><items code="at0047"><items id="description">O procedimento, ou subprocedimento num procedimento com vários componentes, foi realizado.</items><items id="text">Procedimento realizado</items></items><items code="at0048"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Outcome' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">Resultado do procedimento realizado.</items><items id="text">Resultado</items></items><items code="at0049"><items id="comment">Por exemplo: descrição do desempenho e resultados do procedimento, da tentativa abortada ou do cancelamento do procedimento.</items><items id="description">Descrição narrativa sobre o procedimento, conforme apropriado para a etapa do caminho.</items><items id="text">Descrição</items></items><items code="at0053"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0054"><items id="comment">Isto é equivalente ao número de ordem Placer em HL7 v2 especificações.</items><items id="description">O documento de identificação local atribuído ao pedido pelo prestador de cuidados de saúde ou organização que solicita o serviço.</items><items id="text">Identificador do requerente do pedido</items></items><items code="at0055"><items id="description">Detalhes sobre o prestador de cuidados de saúde ou a organização que solicita o serviço.</items><items id="text">Requerente</items></items><items code="at0056"><items id="comment">Isso é equivalente ao número Filler Order Identifier nas especificações HL7 v2.</items><items id="description">O ID atribuído à encomenda pelo prestador de cuidados de saúde ou organização que recebe o pedido de serviço. Isto também é referido como Filler Order Identifier.</items><items id="text">Identificador do destinatário do pedido</items></items><items code="at0057"><items id="description">Informações sobre o prestador de cuidados de saúde ou a organização que recebe o pedido de assistência.</items><items id="text">Recetor</items></items><items code="at0058"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Urgency' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">Urgência do procedimento.</items><items id="text">Urgência</items></items><items code="at0060"><items id="comment">Apenas para utilização em associação com a etapa da via 'Procedimento realizado' e em situações em que o procedimento é repetido em várias ocasiões antes de ser concluído ou há vários componentes em todo o procedimento. Isso pode ser o mesmo que o atributo de tempo RM para a etapa de caminho 'Procedimento concluído'.</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the last component of a multicomponent procedure, was finished. (en)</items><items id="text">*End datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0061"><items id="comment">Apenas para utilização em associação com as etapas do caminho 'Procedimento concluído'.</items><items id="description">O tempo total necessário para concluir o procedimento, que pode incluir o tempo gasto durante a fase ativa do procedimento e o tempo durante o qual o procedimento foi suspenso.</items><items id="text">Duração total</items></items><items code="at0062"><items id="description">Representação multimédia de um procedimento realizado.</items><items id="text">Multimédia</items></items><items code="at0063"><items id="comment">As ocorrências para este elemento de dados são ilimitadas para permitir cenários clínicos tais como a remoção de lesões de pele múltiplas em lugares diferentes, mas onde todos os outros atributos são idênticos. Use esse elemento de dados para registar termos simples ou localizações anatómicas pré-ordenadas. Se os requisitos para o registo da localização anatómica forem determinados no CLUSTER.anatomical_location ou CLUSTER.relative_location dentro do SLOT 'Detalhe do procedimento' neste arquétipo. Se a localização anatómica for incluída no 'Nome do procedimento' por meio de códigos pré-ordenados, esse elemento de dados ficará redundante.</items><items id="description">Identificação do local do corpo para o procedimento.</items><items id="text">Local do corpo</items></items><items code="at0064"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">Extensão</items></items><items code="at0065"><items id="comment">Use esse elemento de dados para registar termos simples ou uma descrição narrativa. Se os requisitos para o registo do método exigirem uma modelagem mais complexa, isso pode ser representado por arquétipos adicionais dentro do SLOT 'Detalhes do procedimento' neste arquétipo. Se o método for incluído no 'Nome do procedimento' com códigos pré-ordenados, esse elemento de dados ficará redundante.</items><items id="description">Identificação do método ou técnica específica para o procedimento.</items><items id="text">Método</items></items><items code="at0066"><items id="comment">Apenas para utilização em associação com a etapa de caminho 'Procedimento agendado'.</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime on which the procedure is intended to be performed. (en)</items><items id="text">*Scheduled datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0067"><items id="comment">Este elemento de dados pragmáticos pode ser usado para apoiar a organização dentro da interface do/a utilizador/a.</items><items id="description">O tipo de procedimento.</items><items id="text">Tipo de procedimento</items></items><items code="at0068"><items id="description">O procedimento, ou subprocedimento num procedimento com vários componentes, foi iniciado.</items><items id="text">Procedimento iniciado</items></items><items code="at0069"><items id="comment">Exemplos: O doente estava agitado, esvaziamento insuficiente do estômago antes da gastroscopia, um tumor nos ductos biliares impossibilitou a passagem da sonda.</items><items id="description">Dificuldades ou problemas encontrados durante a execução do procedimento.</items><items id="text">Dificuldade processual</items></items><items code="at0070"><items id="comment">*For example: 'Failed bowel preparation' or 'Bowel cancer screening'. Coding of the 'Indication' with a terminology is recommended, if available.  This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required. (en)</items><items id="description">A razão clínica ou relacionada ao processo para o procedimento.</items><items id="text">indicação</items></items><items code="at0071"><items id="comment">The same diagnosis, with the same severity, has a different impact on each patient. This relevance qualifier implies adjusting the overall impact of that health problem according to the patient's characteristics.&#13;
For example: Two patients have the same diagnosis. First-degree burn.&#13;
One is a healthy person, the other is a diabetic patient.&#13;
The impact for that problem in a diabetic patient is HIGHER (more risk of infection..., longuer time healing).&#13;
This element is meant to allow for multiple types of impact, including but not limited to: clinical treatment, home functioning, work life.</items><items id="description">Overall assessment of the impact of a health problem for the specific patient. </items><items id="text">Impact</items></items><items code="at0072"><items id="comment">*For example: An operation with curative intent may be planned, while during the operation it is discovered that curative treatment is not possible and the operation is carried out with a palliative intent instead. Coding of the 'Intent' with a terminology is recommended, if available. This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required. (en)</items><items id="description">*The intended outcome of the procedure. (en)</items><items id="text">*Intent (en)</items></items><items code="at0073"><items id="comment">*For example: the knife to skin time. Only for use in association with the 'Procedure performed', 'Procedure suspended', 'Procedure aborted' or 'Procedure completed' pathway steps. This may be the same as the RM 'time' attribute for the 'Procedure commenced' pathway step. (en)</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the first component of a multicomponent procedure, was first started. (en)</items><items id="text">*Start datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0074"><items id="description">*The duration of time between the start of the most recent pathway step for this procedure and the start of the current pathway step. (en)</items><items id="text">*Pathway step duration (en)</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="ru"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">*A clinical activity carried out for screening, investigative, diagnostic, curative, therapeutic, evaluative or palliative purposes.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure(en)</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">*@ internal @(en)</items><items id="text">*Tree(en)</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Procedure name' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">*Identification of the procedure by name.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure name(en)</items></items><items code="at0003"><items id="description">*Structured information about the procedure. Use to capture detailed, structured information about anatomical location, method &amp; technique, equipment used, devices implanted, results, findings etc.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure detail(en)</items></items><items code="at0004"><items id="description">*</items><items id="text">*Procedure planned (en)</items></items><items code="at0005"><items id="description">*Additional narrative about the procedure or care pathway step not captured in other fields. (en)</items><items id="text">*Comment(en)</items></items><items code="at0006"><items id="comment">*Use this data element to record simple terms or precoordinated complications. For example: Hematuria after a kidney biopsy, tissue irritation after insertion of intravenous catheter. If the requirements for recording complication are more complex then use of a specific CLUSTER archetype within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype is advised and this data element becomes redundant. (en)</items><items id="description">*Details about any complication arising from the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Complication(en)</items></items><items code="at0007"><items id="description">*</items><items id="text">*Procedure request sent (en)</items></items><items code="at0014"><items id="comment">*For example: the reason for the cancellation or suspension of the procedure.(en)</items><items id="description">*Reason that the activity or care pathway step for the identified procedure was carried out.(en)</items><items id="text">*Reason(en)</items></items><items code="at0034"><items id="description">*The procedure to be undertaken is planned.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure planned(en)</items></items><items code="at0035"><items id="description">*Request for procedure sent.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure request sent(en)</items></items><items code="at0036"><items id="description">*The procedure has been scheduled.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure scheduled(en)</items></items><items code="at0038"><items id="description">*The procedure has been postponed.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure postponed(en)</items></items><items code="at0039"><items id="description">*The planned procedure has been cancelled prior to commencement.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure cancelled(en)</items></items><items code="at0040"><items id="description">*The procedure has been suspended.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure suspended(en)</items></items><items code="at0041"><items id="description">*The procedure has been aborted.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure aborted(en)</items></items><items code="at0043"><items id="description">*The procedure has been performed and all associated clinical activities completed.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure completed(en)</items></items><items code="at0047"><items id="description">*The procedure, or subprocedure in a multicomponent procedure, has been performed.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure performed(en)</items></items><items code="at0048"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Outcome' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">*Outcome of procedure performed.(en)</items><items id="text">*Outcome(en)</items></items><items code="at0049"><items id="comment">*For example: description about the performance and findings from the the procedure, the aborted attempt or the cancellation of the procedure.(en)</items><items id="description">*Narrative description about the procedure, as appropriate for the pathway step.(en)</items><items id="text">*Description(en)</items></items><items code="at0053"><items id="description">*@ internal @(en)</items><items id="text">*Tree(en)</items></items><items code="at0054"><items id="comment">*This is equivalent to Placer Order Number in HL7 v2 specifications.(en)</items><items id="description">*The local ID assigned to the order by the healthcare provider or organisation requesting the service.(en)</items><items id="text">*Requestor order identifier(en)</items></items><items code="at0055"><items id="description">Подробности о заказчике (организации), запросившей услугу</items><items id="text">Заказчик</items></items><items code="at0056"><items id="comment">*This is equivalent to Filler Order Number in HL7 v2 specifications.(en)</items><items id="description">*The ID assigned to the order by the healthcare provider or organisation receiving the request for service. This is also referred to as Filler Order Identifier.(en)</items><items id="text">*Receiver order identifier(en)</items></items><items code="at0057"><items id="description">Подробные сведение об организации, получившей заявку на выполнение процедуры</items><items id="text">Исполнитель</items></items><items code="at0058"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Urgency' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">*Urgency of the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Urgency(en)</items></items><items code="at0060"><items id="comment">*Only for use in association with the 'Procedure performed' pathway step, and in situations where the procedure is repeated on multiple occasions before being completed or there are multiple components to the whole procedure. This may be the same as the RM time attribute for the 'Procedure completed' pathway step.(en)</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the last component of a multicomponent procedure, was finished. (en)</items><items id="text">*End datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0061"><items id="comment">*Only for use in association with the 'Procedure completed' pathway steps.(en)</items><items id="description">*The total amount of time taken to complete the procedure, which may include time spent during the active phase of the procedure plus time during which the procedure was suspended.(en)</items><items id="text">*Total duration(en)</items></items><items code="at0062"><items id="description">*Mulitimedia representation of a performed procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Multimedia(en)</items></items><items code="at0063"><items id="comment">*Occurrences for this data element are unbounded to allow for clinical scenarios such as removing multiple skin lesions in different places, but where all of the other attributes are identical. Use this data element to record simple terms or precoordinated anatomical locations. If the requirements for recording the anatomical location are determined at run-time by the application or require more complex modelling such as relative locations then use the CLUSTER.anatomical_location or CLUSTER.relative_location within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype. If the anatomical location is included in the 'Procedure name' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant.(en)</items><items id="description">*Identification of the body site for the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Body site(en)</items></items><items code="at0064"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">*Extension(en)</items></items><items code="at0065"><items id="comment">*Use this data element to record simple terms or a narrative description. If the requirements for recording the method require more complex modelling then this can be represented by additional archetypes within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype. If the method is included in the 'Procedure name' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant.(en)</items><items id="description">*Identification of specific method or technique for the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Method(en)</items></items><items code="at0066"><items id="comment">*Only for use in association with the 'Procedure scheduled' pathway step.(en)</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime on which the procedure is intended to be performed. (en)</items><items id="text">*Scheduled datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0067"><items id="comment">*This pragmatic data element may be used to support organisation within the user interface.(en)</items><items id="description">*The type of procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure type(en)</items></items><items code="at0068"><items id="description">*The procedure, or subprocedure in a multicomponent procedure, has been commenced.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure commenced(en)</items></items><items code="at0069"><items id="description">*Difficulties or issues encountered during the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedural difficulty(en)</items></items><items code="at0070"><items id="comment">*For example: 'Failed bowel preparation' or 'Bowel cancer screening'. Coding of the 'Indication' with a terminology is recommended, if available.  This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required. (en)</items><items id="description">*The clinical or process-related reason for the procedure. (en)</items><items id="text">*Indication (en)</items></items><items code="at0071"><items id="comment">The same diagnosis, with the same severity, has a different impact on each patient. This relevance qualifier implies adjusting the overall impact of that health problem according to the patient's characteristics.&#13;
For example: Two patients have the same diagnosis. First-degree burn.&#13;
One is a healthy person, the other is a diabetic patient.&#13;
The impact for that problem in a diabetic patient is HIGHER (more risk of infection..., longuer time healing).&#13;
This element is meant to allow for multiple types of impact, including but not limited to: clinical treatment, home functioning, work life.</items><items id="description">Overall assessment of the impact of a health problem for the specific patient. </items><items id="text">Impact</items></items><items code="at0072"><items id="comment">*For example: An operation with curative intent may be planned, while during the operation it is discovered that curative treatment is not possible and the operation is carried out with a palliative intent instead. Coding of the 'Intent' with a terminology is recommended, if available. This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required. (en)</items><items id="description">*The intended outcome of the procedure. (en)</items><items id="text">*Intent (en)</items></items><items code="at0073"><items id="comment">*For example: the knife to skin time. Only for use in association with the 'Procedure performed', 'Procedure suspended', 'Procedure aborted' or 'Procedure completed' pathway steps. This may be the same as the RM 'time' attribute for the 'Procedure commenced' pathway step. (en)</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the first component of a multicomponent procedure, was first started. (en)</items><items id="text">*Start datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0074"><items id="description">*The duration of time between the start of the most recent pathway step for this procedure and the start of the current pathway step. (en)</items><items id="text">*Pathway step duration (en)</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="sl"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">*A clinical activity carried out for screening, investigative, diagnostic, curative, therapeutic, evaluative or palliative purposes.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure(en)</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">*@ internal @(en)</items><items id="text">*Tree(en)</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Procedure name' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">*Identification of the procedure by name.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure name(en)</items></items><items code="at0003"><items id="description">*Structured information about the procedure. Use to capture detailed, structured information about anatomical location, method &amp; technique, equipment used, devices implanted, results, findings etc.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure detail(en)</items></items><items code="at0004"><items id="description">*</items><items id="text">*Procedure planned (en)</items></items><items code="at0005"><items id="description">*Additional narrative about the procedure or care pathway step not captured in other fields. (en)</items><items id="text">*Comment(en)</items></items><items code="at0006"><items id="comment">*Use this data element to record simple terms or precoordinated complications. For example: Hematuria after a kidney biopsy, tissue irritation after insertion of intravenous catheter. If the requirements for recording complication are more complex then use of a specific CLUSTER archetype within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype is advised and this data element becomes redundant. (en)</items><items id="description">*Details about any complication arising from the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Complication(en)</items></items><items code="at0007"><items id="description">*</items><items id="text">*Procedure request sent (en)</items></items><items code="at0014"><items id="comment">*For example: the reason for the cancellation or suspension of the procedure.(en)</items><items id="description">*Reason that the activity or care pathway step for the identified procedure was carried out.(en)</items><items id="text">*Reason(en)</items></items><items code="at0034"><items id="description">*The procedure to be undertaken is planned.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure planned(en)</items></items><items code="at0035"><items id="description">*Request for procedure sent.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure request sent(en)</items></items><items code="at0036"><items id="description">*The procedure has been scheduled.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure scheduled(en)</items></items><items code="at0038"><items id="description">*The procedure has been postponed.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure postponed(en)</items></items><items code="at0039"><items id="description">*The planned procedure has been cancelled prior to commencement.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure cancelled(en)</items></items><items code="at0040"><items id="description">*The procedure has been suspended.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure suspended(en)</items></items><items code="at0041"><items id="description">*The procedure has been aborted.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure aborted(en)</items></items><items code="at0043"><items id="description">*The procedure has been performed and all associated clinical activities completed.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure completed(en)</items></items><items code="at0047"><items id="description">*The procedure, or subprocedure in a multicomponent procedure, has been performed.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure performed(en)</items></items><items code="at0048"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Outcome' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">*Outcome of procedure performed.(en)</items><items id="text">*Outcome(en)</items></items><items code="at0049"><items id="comment">*For example: description about the performance and findings from the the procedure, the aborted attempt or the cancellation of the procedure.(en)</items><items id="description">*Narrative description about the procedure, as appropriate for the pathway step.(en)</items><items id="text">*Description(en)</items></items><items code="at0053"><items id="description">*@ internal @(en)</items><items id="text">*Tree(en)</items></items><items code="at0054"><items id="comment">*This is equivalent to Placer Order Number in HL7 v2 specifications.(en)</items><items id="description">*The local ID assigned to the order by the healthcare provider or organisation requesting the service.(en)</items><items id="text">*Requestor order identifier(en)</items></items><items code="at0055"><items id="description">Kdo je naročil aktivnost, posameznik ali organizacija</items><items id="text">Naročnik</items></items><items code="at0056"><items id="comment">*This is equivalent to Filler Order Number in HL7 v2 specifications.(en)</items><items id="description">*The ID assigned to the order by the healthcare provider or organisation receiving the request for service. This is also referred to as Filler Order Identifier.(en)</items><items id="text">*Receiver order identifier(en)</items></items><items code="at0057"><items id="description">Prejemnik naročila za izvedbo aktivnosti</items><items id="text">Prejemnik</items></items><items code="at0058"><items id="comment">*Coding of the 'Urgency' with a terminology is recommended, if available. (en)</items><items id="description">*Urgency of the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Urgency(en)</items></items><items code="at0060"><items id="comment">*Only for use in association with the 'Procedure performed' pathway step, and in situations where the procedure is repeated on multiple occasions before being completed or there are multiple components to the whole procedure. This may be the same as the RM time attribute for the 'Procedure completed' pathway step.(en)</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the last component of a multicomponent procedure, was finished. (en)</items><items id="text">*End datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0061"><items id="comment">*Only for use in association with the 'Procedure completed' pathway steps.(en)</items><items id="description">*The total amount of time taken to complete the procedure, which may include time spent during the active phase of the procedure plus time during which the procedure was suspended.(en)</items><items id="text">*Total duration(en)</items></items><items code="at0062"><items id="description">*Mulitimedia representation of a performed procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Multimedia(en)</items></items><items code="at0063"><items id="comment">*Occurrences for this data element are unbounded to allow for clinical scenarios such as removing multiple skin lesions in different places, but where all of the other attributes are identical. Use this data element to record simple terms or precoordinated anatomical locations. If the requirements for recording the anatomical location are determined at run-time by the application or require more complex modelling such as relative locations then use the CLUSTER.anatomical_location or CLUSTER.relative_location within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype. If the anatomical location is included in the 'Procedure name' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant.(en)</items><items id="description">*Identification of the body site for the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Body site(en)</items></items><items code="at0064"><items id="comment">*For example: local information requirements; or additional metadata to align with FHIR. (en)</items><items id="description">*Additional information required to extend the model with local content or to align with other reference models or formalisms. (en)</items><items id="text">*Extension(en)</items></items><items code="at0065"><items id="comment">*Use this data element to record simple terms or a narrative description. If the requirements for recording the method require more complex modelling then this can be represented by additional archetypes within the 'Procedure detail' SLOT in this archetype. If the method is included in the 'Procedure name' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant.(en)</items><items id="description">*Identification of specific method or technique for the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Method(en)</items></items><items code="at0066"><items id="comment">*Only for use in association with the 'Procedure scheduled' pathway step.(en)</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime on which the procedure is intended to be performed. (en)</items><items id="text">*Scheduled datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0067"><items id="comment">*This pragmatic data element may be used to support organisation within the user interface.(en)</items><items id="description">*The type of procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure type(en)</items></items><items code="at0068"><items id="description">*The procedure, or subprocedure in a multicomponent procedure, has been commenced.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedure commenced(en)</items></items><items code="at0069"><items id="description">*Difficulties or issues encountered during the procedure.(en)</items><items id="text">*Procedural difficulty(en)</items></items><items code="at0070"><items id="comment">*For example: 'Failed bowel preparation' or 'Bowel cancer screening'. Coding of the 'Indication' with a terminology is recommended, if available.  This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required. (en)</items><items id="description">*The clinical or process-related reason for the procedure. (en)</items><items id="text">*Indication (en)</items></items><items code="at0071"><items id="comment">The same diagnosis, with the same severity, has a different impact on each patient. This relevance qualifier implies adjusting the overall impact of that health problem according to the patient's characteristics.&#13;
For example: Two patients have the same diagnosis. First-degree burn.&#13;
One is a healthy person, the other is a diabetic patient.&#13;
The impact for that problem in a diabetic patient is HIGHER (more risk of infection..., longuer time healing).&#13;
This element is meant to allow for multiple types of impact, including but not limited to: clinical treatment, home functioning, work life.</items><items id="description">Overall assessment of the impact of a health problem for the specific patient. </items><items id="text">Impact</items></items><items code="at0072"><items id="comment">*For example: An operation with curative intent may be planned, while during the operation it is discovered that curative treatment is not possible and the operation is carried out with a palliative intent instead. Coding of the 'Intent' with a terminology is recommended, if available. This data element allows multiple occurrences to enable the user to record multiple responses, if required. (en)</items><items id="description">*The intended outcome of the procedure. (en)</items><items id="text">*Intent (en)</items></items><items code="at0073"><items id="comment">*For example: the knife to skin time. Only for use in association with the 'Procedure performed', 'Procedure suspended', 'Procedure aborted' or 'Procedure completed' pathway steps. This may be the same as the RM 'time' attribute for the 'Procedure commenced' pathway step. (en)</items><items id="description">*The date or datetime when the entire procedure, or the first component of a multicomponent procedure, was first started. (en)</items><items id="text">*Start datetime (en)</items></items><items code="at0074"><items id="description">*The duration of time between the start of the most recent pathway step for this procedure and the start of the current pathway step. (en)</items><items id="text">*Pathway step duration (en)</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="sv"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">En klinisk aktivitet utförd för screening-, undersökande, diagnostiska, botande, terapeutiska, utvärderande eller palliativa ändamål.</items><items id="text">Åtgärd</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">Om möjligt, koda "benämning på åtgärd" med en terminologi.</items><items id="description">Åtgärdens benämning.</items><items id="text">Benämning på åtgärd</items></items><items code="at0003"><items id="comment">Används för att fånga detaljerad, strukturerad information om anatomisk plats, metod och teknik, utrustning som används, implanterat såsom enheter eller utrustning, resultat, fynd m.m.</items><items id="description">Strukturerad information om åtgärden.</items><items id="text">Åtgärdsdetaljer</items></items><items code="at0004"><items id="description">Den åtgärd som ska genomföras är planerad.</items><items id="text">Åtgärd planerad</items></items><items code="at0005"><items id="description">Kommentarer om åtgärden eller processteget som inte beskrivs i övriga datafält.</items><items id="text">Kommentar</items></items><items code="at0006"><items id="comment">Använd detta datafält för att registrera enkla eller prekoordinerade termer för komplikationer.&#13;
&#13;
Exempelvis hematuri efter njurbiopsi eller vävnadsirritation efter insättning av en intravenös kateter. Om komplikationen behöver dokumenteras mer detaljerat rekommenderas användning av en specifik CLUSTER-arketyp i SLOT "Åtgärdsdetaljer". I sådana fall behöver detta datafält inte användas.</items><items id="description">Detaljer om eventuella komplikationer som uppstår från åtgärden.</items><items id="text">Komplikation</items></items><items code="at0007"><items id="description">Förfrågan om åtgärd är skickad.&#13;
</items><items id="text">Förfrågan om åtgärd skickad</items></items><items code="at0014"><items id="comment">Exempelvis anledningen till att åtgärden är i processteget pausad eller avbruten.</items><items id="description">Anledning till att nytt processteg för åtgärden dokumenterats.</items><items id="text">Anledning</items></items><items code="at0034"><items id="comment">(Var: Den åtgärd som ska utföras är planerad.)</items><items id="description">Detta steg har upphört att gälla eftersom det felaktigt var associerat med status "initial". Använd det nya steget "Åtgärd planerad" (at0004) som är korrekt associerat med status "planerad" . &#13;
</items><items id="text">X - Åtgärd planerad</items></items><items code="at0035"><items id="comment">(Var: Åtgärdsförfrågan skickad.)</items><items id="description">Detta steg har upphört att gälla eftersom det felaktigt var associerat med status "initial". Använd det nya steget "Åtgärdsförfrågan skickad" (at0007) som är korrekt associerat med status "planerad".</items><items id="text">X - Förfrågan om åtgärd skickad</items></items><items code="at0036"><items id="description">Åtgärden är bokad.</items><items id="text">Åtgärd bokad</items></items><items code="at0038"><items id="description">Åtgärden är uppskjuten.&#13;
</items><items id="text">Åtgärd uppskjuten</items></items><items code="at0039"><items id="description">Den planerade åtgärden är inställd.</items><items id="text">Åtgärd inställd</items></items><items code="at0040"><items id="description">Åtgärden är pausad.</items><items id="text">Åtgärd pausad</items></items><items code="at0041"><items id="description">Åtgärden är avbruten.&#13;
</items><items id="text">Åtgärd avbruten</items></items><items code="at0043"><items id="description">Åtgärden och alla tillhörande kliniska aktiviteter är slutförda.</items><items id="text">Åtgärd slutförd</items></items><items code="at0047"><items id="description">Åtgärden är utförd.</items><items id="text">Åtgärd utförd</items></items><items code="at0048"><items id="comment">Om möjligt, koda "resultat" med en terminologi.</items><items id="description">Resultat av genomförd åtgärd.</items><items id="text">Resultat</items></items><items code="at0049"><items id="comment">Exempelvis, en beskrivning av åtgärdens utförande och dess fynd, den avbrutna åtgärden eller den inställda åtgärden.</items><items id="description">Beskrivning av åtgärden, anpassad till det aktuella processteget.</items><items id="text">Beskrivning</items></items><items code="at0053"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0054"><items id="comment">Detta motsvarar Place Order Number i specifikationerna för HL7 v2.</items><items id="description">Beställnings-ID definierat av den aktör som är avsändare av förfrågan av tjänst.</items><items id="text">Beställnings-ID hos avsändare</items></items><items code="at0055"><items id="description">Detaljer om den aktör som efterfrågar tjänsten.</items><items id="text">Beställare</items></items><items code="at0056"><items id="comment">Detta motsvarar Filler Order Number i specifikationerna för HL7 v2.</items><items id="description">Beställnings-ID definierat av den aktör som tar emot förfrågan av tjänsten.</items><items id="text">Betällnings-ID hos mottagare</items></items><items code="at0057"><items id="description">Detaljer om den aktör som tar emot förfrågan av tjänsten.</items><items id="text">Mottagare</items></items><items code="at0058"><items id="comment">Om möjligt, koda "brådskandegrad" med en terminologi.</items><items id="description">Åtgärdens brådskandegrad.</items><items id="text">Brådskandegrad</items></items><items code="at0060"><items id="comment">Kan endast användas i samband med steget "Åtgärd utförd" och i situationer där åtgärden upprepas vid flera tillfällen innan den avslutas eller om det finns flera delåtgärder i hela åtgärden. Detta kan vara detsamma som referensmodellens attribut för steget "Åtgärd slutförd".</items><items id="description">Det datum eller den tidpunkt, då hela åtgärden avslutades eller det sista delmomentet i en åtgärd som består av flera delmoment.</items><items id="text">Sluttidpunkt</items></items><items code="at0061"><items id="comment">Kan endast användas i samband med steget "Åtgärd slutförd".</items><items id="description">Den totala tid som krävs för att utföra åtgärden, vilket kan inkludera tid som tillbringats under den aktiva fasen av åtgärden plus den tid under vilken åtgärden pausades.</items><items id="text">Total varaktighet</items></items><items code="at0062"><items id="description">Multimedierepresentation av utförd åtgärd.</items><items id="text">Multimedia</items></items><items code="at0063"><items id="comment">Förekomsten av detta datafält är obegränsat för att möjliggöra kliniska scenarier som att ta bort flera hudförändringar på olika lokalisationer, men där alla andra attribut är identiska. Använd detta datafält för att dokumentera enkla termer eller prekoordinerade kroppslokalisationer. Om kraven på dokumentation av den lokalisationen bestäms vid körning av applikationen eller kräver mer komplex modellering, till exempel relativa lokalisationer (exempelvis 3 cm ovanför vänster knä), använd CLUSTER.anatomical_location eller CLUSTER.relative_location i SLOT "Åtgärdsdetaljer" i denna arketyp. Om kroppslokalisationen ingår i "Benämning på åtgärd" genom prekoordinerade koder blir detta datafält överflödigt.</items><items id="description">Identifiering av anatomisk plats för åtgärden.</items><items id="text">Kroppslokalisation</items></items><items code="at0064"><items id="comment">Exempelvis lokala informationskrav eller metadata för anpassning till FHIR.</items><items id="description">Plats för tilläggsinformation som krävs för lokala anpassningar eller anpassning till andra referensmodeller eller formella krav.</items><items id="text">Tilläggsinformation</items></items><items code="at0065"><items id="comment">Använd detta datafält för att dokumentera metoden. Om kraven för dokumentation av metoden kräver mer komplex modellering kan detta representeras av ytterligare arketyper i SLOT "Åtgärdsdetalj" i denna arketyp. Om metoden ingår i "Benämning på åtgärd" genom prekoordinerade koder blir detta datafält överflödigt.</items><items id="description">Identifiering av specifik metod eller teknik för åtgärden.</items><items id="text">Metod</items></items><items code="at0066"><items id="comment">Ska endast användas i samband med steget "Åtgärd bokad".</items><items id="description">Det datum eller den tidpunkt som åtgärden är planerad att utföras.</items><items id="text">Planerad tidpunkt</items></items><items code="at0067"><items id="comment">Detta datafält kan användas för att tydliggöra användargränssnittets struktur.</items><items id="description">Typ av åtgärd.</items><items id="text">Åtgärdstyp</items></items><items code="at0068"><items id="description">Åtgärden är påbörjad.</items><items id="text">Åtgärd påbörjad</items></items><items code="at0069"><items id="comment">Exempelvis patienten var upprörd, otillräcklig tömning av magsäcken före gastroskopi, en tumör i gallgångarna gjorde det omöjligt att passera igenom med gastroskop.</items><items id="description">Svårigheter eller problem som uppstår under genomförandet av åtgärden.</items><items id="text">Svårigheter med åtgärd</items></items><items code="at0070"><items id="comment">Exempelvis "Misslyckad tarmförberedelse" eller "Screening för kolorektalcancer". Om möjligt, koda "indikation" till en terminologi. Detta datafält kan vid behov registreras flera gånger för att möjliggöra dokumentation av flera indikationer.</items><items id="description">Den kliniska eller processrelaterade orsaken till åtgärden.</items><items id="text">Indikation</items></items><items code="at0071"><items id="comment">Samma åtgärd, med samma svårighetsgrad eller resultat, kan ha olika påverkan för olika patienter. Denna relevansfaktor innebär att den samlade påverkan av åtgärden eller resultatet bedöms utifrån patientens individuella förutsättningar.&#13;
&#13;
Exempelvis kan två patienter ha genomgått samma åtgärd med samma resultat: osteosyntes av lillfingret på den icke-dominanta handen. Den ena patienten arbetar som trädgårdsarbetare eller byggnadsarbetare, den andra är pianist. Påverkan av åtgärden är större för pianisten, exempelvis genom längre sjukskrivning och behov av full funktionell rehabilitering för att kunna återgå till arbetet som har höga krav på finmotorik.&#13;
&#13;
Detta datafält är avsett att möjliggöra registrering av olika typer av påverkan, inklusive men inte begränsat till påverkan på behandling, funktion i hemmet eller arbetsliv.</items><items id="description">Bedömning av vilken påverkan en åtgärd eller dess resultat har på den enskilda patienten.</items><items id="text">Påverkan</items></items><items code="at0072"><items id="comment">Exempelvis en operation med kurativ avsikt kan planeras, men under operationen visar det sig att kurativ behandling inte är möjlig och att ingreppet istället genomförs med palliativ avsikt. Om möjligt, koda "avsikt" med en terminologi. Detta datafält kan vid behov registreras flera gånger för att möjliggöra dokumentation av flera indikationer.</items><items id="description">Det avsedda resultatet av åtgärden.</items><items id="text">Avsikt</items></items><items code="at0073"><items id="comment">Exempelvis tidpunkten för första incisionen ("knife-to-skin time"). Används endast tillsammans med processtegen "Åtgärd utförd", "Åtgärd pausad", "Åtgärd avbruten" eller "Åtgärd slutförd". Detta värde kan vara detsamma som referensmodellens attribut "time" för processteget "Åtgärd påbörjad".</items><items id="description">Det datum eller den tidpunkt, då hela åtgärden påbörjades eller den första delen av en åtgärd som består av flera delmoment.</items><items id="text">Starttidpunkt</items></items><items code="at0074"><items id="description">Tidsperioden mellan starten av det senast registrerade processteget för denna åtgärd och starten av det aktuella processteget.</items><items id="text">Duration för processteg</items></items></term_definitions><term_definitions language="zh-cn"><items code="at0000"><items id="description">为了实现评估类、探查类、筛查类、诊断类、治愈类、疗法类或姑息治疗类等目的而开展的临床活动。</items><items id="text">操作</items></items><items code="at0001"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0002"><items id="comment">如果可用，建议采用统一的术语集对“操作名称”加以编码。</items><items id="description">利用名称对于此项操作进行的标识。</items><items id="text">操作名称</items></items><items code="at0003"><items id="comment">用于记录操作相关的详细的结构化信息，包括解剖学位置、方法与技术方法、所采用的设备、所植入的器械/装置、结果、发现/所见等。</items><items id="description">关于此项操作的结构化信息。</items><items id="text">操作详情</items></items><items code="at0004"><items id="description">计划有待开展/执行/实施的操作。</items><items id="text">操作已编制计划</items></items><items code="at0005"><items id="description">额外关于此项操作或照护路径步骤的，其他字段并未涵盖的叙述性说明。</items><items id="text">注释</items></items><items code="at0006"><items id="comment">利用此数据元来记录简单的术语或先组配型的并发症。例如：肾活检后血尿、静脉导管置入后组织刺激。如果记录并发症的需求更为复杂，则建议在此原始型的操作详情槽位“Procedure detail”之中使用特定的群簇型（CLUSTER）原始型，而此时则不再需要本数据元。</items><items id="description">关于此项操作所引发的任何并发症的详情。</items><items id="text">并发症</items></items><items code="at0007"><items id="description">已发送关于当前操作的请求。</items><items id="text">操作请求已发送</items></items><items code="at0014"><items id="comment">例如：关于取消或暂停当前操作的原因。</items><items id="description">关于针对当前操作实际开展/执行此项活动或照护服务路径步骤的原因。</items><items id="text">原因</items></items><items code="at0034"><items id="comment">（原描述：计划有待开展/执行/实施的操作。）</items><items id="description">目前已弃用此路径步骤，因其错误地关联了“初始”（initial）状态 —— 请采用新的“操作已编制计划”（Procedure planned，编码：at0004）路径步骤，该步骤正确地关联了“已计划”（planned）状态。</items><items id="text">X - 操作已编制计划</items></items><items code="at0035"><items id="comment">（原描述：已发送关于当前操作的请求。）</items><items id="description">目前已弃用此路径步骤，因其错误地关联了“初始”（initial）状态 —— 请采用新的“操作请求已发送”（Procedure request sent，编码：at0007）路径步骤，该步骤正确地关联了“已计划”（planned）状态。</items><items id="text">X - 操作请求已发送</items></items><items code="at0036"><items id="description">目前已对此项操作进行了排程。</items><items id="text">操作已排程</items></items><items code="at0038"><items id="description">目前已延期此项操作。</items><items id="text">操作已延期</items></items><items code="at0039"><items id="description">已计划的操作在开始之前已被取消。</items><items id="text">操作已取消</items></items><items code="at0040"><items id="description">目前已暂停此项操作。</items><items id="text">操作已暂停</items></items><items code="at0041"><items id="description">目前已中止此项操作。</items><items id="text">操作已中止</items></items><items code="at0043"><items id="description">目前已执行此项操作，且所有相关的临床活动均已完成。</items><items id="text">操作已完成</items></items><items code="at0047"><items id="description">目前已执行此项操作（或多组成部分操作之中的此项子操作）。</items><items id="text">操作已执行</items></items><items code="at0048"><items id="comment">如果可用，建议采用统一的术语集对“紧急程度”加以编码。</items><items id="description">已执行操作的结局。</items><items id="text">结局</items></items><items code="at0049"><items id="comment">例如：关于此项操作的执行情况与发现/所见、已中止的尝试或此项操作的取消的描述。</items><items id="description">对于此项操作进行的，适合于当前路径步骤的叙述性描述。</items><items id="text">描述</items></items><items code="at0053"><items id="description">@ internal @</items><items id="text">Tree</items></items><items code="at0054"><items id="comment">该标识符等同于HL7 v2标准中的“申请方医嘱编号”（Placer Order Number）。</items><items id="description">申请此项服务的健康医疗服务提供方或机构为此项医嘱所分配的本地标识符。</items><items id="text">申请方医嘱标识符</items></items><items code="at0055"><items id="description">关于申请此项服务的健康医疗服务提供方或机构的相关详情。</items><items id="text">申请方</items></items><items code="at0056"><items id="comment">该标识符等同于 HL7 v2 标准之中的“执行方医嘱编号”（Filler Order Number）。</items><items id="description">由接收服务请求的健康医疗服务提供方或机构为此项医嘱所分配的标识符，也称为“执行方医嘱标识符”（Filler Order Identifier）。</items><items id="text">接收方医嘱标识符</items></items><items code="at0057"><items id="description">关于接收服务请求的健康医疗服务提供方或机构的相关详情。</items><items id="text">接收方</items></items><items code="at0058"><items id="comment">如果可用，建议采用统一的术语集对“紧急程度”加以编码。</items><items id="description">此项操作的紧急程度。</items><items id="text">紧急程度</items></items><items code="at0060"><items id="comment">仅仅旨在与“操作已执行”路径步骤联合运用，且适用于以下场景：操作在完成之前需多次重复进行，或整个操作包含多个组成部分。该时间可能与“操作已完成”路径步骤的参考模型（RM）时间属性“time”相同。</items><items id="description">整个操作完成/结束时的日期或日期时间，或者是多组成部分操作之中最后一个组成部分完成/结束时的日期或日期时间。</items><items id="text">结束日期时间</items></items><items code="at0061"><items id="comment">仅仅旨在与“操作已完成”（Procedure completed）路径步骤联合运用。</items><items id="description">完成此项操作所实际花费的总时间，可能包括操作执行阶段所花费的时间以及操作暂停期间所流逝的时间。</items><items id="text">总时长</items></items><items code="at0062"><items id="description">关于所执行的操作的多媒体呈现资料。</items><items id="text">多媒体</items></items><items code="at0063"><items id="comment">该数据元的出现次数不限，以便适配需对不同部位进行相同操作的临床场景（例如，切除不同部位的多个皮肤病变，而操作的其余所有属性均相同）。请采用本数据元来记录简单的术语或先组配型的解剖学位置。若解剖学位置的记录需求需要的是应用程序在运行时确定，或者是需更为复杂的建模（如相对位置），则应当采用本原始型操作详情槽位（Procedure detail）之中的群簇类解剖学位置原始型（CLUSTER.anatomical_location）或群簇类相对位置原始型（CLUSTER.relative_location）。若已经利用先组配型代码将解剖学位置信息包含在“操作名称”数据元当中，则无需填写本数据元。</items><items id="description">对于此项操作所针对的身体部位的标识。</items><items id="text">身体部位</items></items><items code="at0064"><items id="comment">例如：本地信息需求；或用于与FHIR保持一致时所需的额外元数据。</items><items id="description">为了利益本地内容来扩展模型或与其他参考模型或形式化体系保持一致时所需的附加信息。&#13;
&#13;
</items><items id="text">扩展</items></items><items code="at0065"><items id="comment">请采用本数据元来记录简单的术语或叙述性的描述。若方法的记录需求需要更为复杂的建模，则可在本原始型之中的操作详情槽位（Procedure detail）内利用其他的原始型来表达。若已经利用先组配型代码将方法信息包含在“操作名称”数据元当中，则无需填写本数据元。</items><items id="description">对于此项操作所采用的特定方法或技术方法的标识。</items><items id="text">方法</items></items><items code="at0066"><items id="comment">仅仅旨在与“已排程的操作”（Procedure scheduled）路径步骤联合运用。</items><items id="description">预定执行此项操作的日期或日期时间。</items><items id="text">预定日期时间</items></items><items code="at0067"><items id="comment">这一实用性数据元可用于支持实现用户界面之中的内容分类组织。</items><items id="description">此项操作的类型。</items><items id="text">操作类型</items></items><items code="at0068"><items id="description">此项操作（或多组成部分操作之中的此项子操作）目前已开始。</items><items id="text">操作已开始</items></items><items code="at0069"><items id="comment">示例：患者烦躁不安、胃镜检查前胃排空不充分、胆管内肿瘤导致内镜无法通过。</items><items id="description">执行此项操作过程中所遇到的困难或问题。</items><items id="text">操作难度</items></items><items code="at0070"><items id="comment">例如：“肠道准备失败”或“结直肠癌筛查”。如果可用，建议采用统一的术语集对“适应证”加以编码。如果需要，此数据元还允许出现多次，以便用户记录多个答案选项/应答。</items><items id="description">此项操作的临床原因/理由或流程相关原因/理由。</items><items id="text">适应证</items></items><items code="at0071"><items id="comment">相同的操作，即便具有相同的严重程度或结局，对每位患者的影响也可能有所不同。这一相关因素涉及到依据患者的特点/特征来调整此项操作或其结局的整体影响程度。&#13;
&#13;
例如：两名患者接受了相同的操作，并获得了相同的结局：对这两位患者的非优势手第五指均进行的是骨缝合修复术（osteosynthesis repair）。&#13;
&#13;
其中，一位患者是园丁或建筑工人，而另一位则是钢琴家。&#13;
&#13;
此项操作对钢琴家的影响更大（病假时间更长，需要完全的功能康复，以适应工作对精细动作的高要求）。&#13;
&#13;
此数据元旨在允许记录多种类型的影响，包括但不仅限于：临床治疗、居家功能发挥或工作生活。</items><items id="description">对于某一操作或其结局对特定患者所产生影响的评估。</items><items id="text">影响</items></items><items code="at0072"><items id="comment">例如：原本可能计划进行的是以治愈/根治为目的的手术，但在手术过程中却发现无法进行根治性治疗，于是改为以姑息性目的进行手术。如果可用，建议采用统一的术语集对“目的”加以编码。如果需要，此数据元还允许出现多次，以便用户记录多个答案选项/应答。</items><items id="description">操作的预期结果。</items><items id="text">目的</items></items><items code="at0073"><items id="comment">例如：手术切皮时间。仅仅旨在用于与“操作已执行”、“操作已暂停”、“操作已中止”或“操作已完成”路径步骤联合运用。此时间可能与“操作已开始”路径步骤的参考模型（RM）时间属性“time”相同。</items><items id="description">整个操作开始时的日期或日期时间，或者是多组成部分操作之中第一个组成部分的首次开始日期或日期时间。</items><items id="text">开始日期时间</items></items><items code="at0074"><items id="description">此项操作最新一个路径步骤的开始时间与当前路径步骤的开始时间之间的持续时长。</items><items id="text">路径步骤持续时长</items></items></term_definitions></component_ontologies></template>